age difference between us.

255
00:08:47,745 --> 00:08:49,269
- [Tom Servo] She's
drinking fermented Yoohoo.

256
00:08:49,269 --> 00:08:51,298
- If you were five
years older I'd jump ya.

257
00:08:51,298 --> 00:08:52,747
- [Mike] Well I got
cables in the car, ma'am.

258
00:08:52,747 --> 00:08:53,726
- Terry!

259
00:08:53,726 --> 00:08:55,551
Hey, you look great.

260
00:08:55,551 --> 00:08:56,778
Doesn't she, Mrs. Kester?

261
00:08:56,778 --> 00:08:58,863
- I'm ready for some muskrat lovin'.

262
00:08:58,863 --> 00:08:59,871
- Yes.

263
00:08:59,871 --> 00:09:00,992
- Come on, Terry.

264
00:09:00,992 --> 00:09:03,617
- [Tom Servo] Bye little slutster.

265
00:09:03,617 --> 00:09:06,293
- [Mike] Saved a lot
buying the old Gein place.

266
00:09:06,293 --> 00:09:08,095
- I suppose I should move grandma's body

267
00:09:08,095 --> 00:09:09,678
out of the den now.

268
00:09:10,746 --> 00:09:12,960
- [Tom Servo] Fore!

269
00:09:12,960 --> 00:09:13,793
(telephone ringing)

270
00:09:13,793 --> 00:09:15,293
- [Tom Servo] Doh!

271
00:09:16,950 --> 00:09:18,252
- Hello, Sheriff's Office.

272
00:09:18,252 --> 00:09:20,175
- Professor made a
toaster out of coconuts?

273
00:09:20,175 --> 00:09:21,008
Why?

274
00:09:21,008 --> 00:09:22,785
- I see, uh huh.

275
00:09:22,785 --> 00:09:23,927
Disturbing the peace?

276
00:09:23,927 --> 00:09:25,095
- [Tom Servo] We could do that.

277
00:09:25,095 --> 00:09:27,041
- Yes ma'am, that's an arrestable offense.

278
00:09:27,041 --> 00:09:29,253
- [Mike] Repeat what you
say to provide exposition?

279
00:09:29,253 --> 00:09:31,444
- No, the law does not apply to preaching.

280
00:09:31,444 --> 00:09:34,201
- Hell fire and brimstone!

281
00:09:34,201 --> 00:09:35,948
That is what is in store for you.

282
00:09:35,948 --> 00:09:37,266
- Dennis Rodman, listening?

283
00:09:37,266 --> 00:09:38,424
- It's right here.

284
00:09:38,424 --> 00:09:40,406
Psalms 11 verse six,

285
00:09:40,406 --> 00:09:45,090
"Upon the wicked he shall
rain fire and brimstone!"

286
00:09:45,090 --> 00:09:48,335
- [Tom Servo] Oh, and spiders!

287
00:09:48,335 --> 00:09:49,684
- I need one room in Las Vegas

288
00:09:49,684 --> 00:09:50,977
and a lot of liquor please.

289
00:09:50,977 --> 00:09:53,281
- Dutch, this is Ev.

290
00:09:53,281 --> 00:09:55,803
There's not a drop of
booze left in this house.

291
00:09:55,803 --> 00:09:57,156
I just can't stand it.

292
00:09:57,156 --> 00:09:58,565
I'm really desperate.

293
00:09:58,565 --> 00:09:59,908
Would you bring me something?

294
00:09:59,908 --> 00:10:02,302
- [Crow] This is not the
purpose of 9-1-1, ma'am.

295
00:10:02,302 --> 00:10:04,036
- [Tom Servo] A pony
cake should tide me over.

296
00:10:04,036 --> 00:10:05,285
- Oh, thanks Dutch.

297
00:10:05,285 --> 00:10:06,118
Listen,

298
00:10:06,973 --> 00:10:09,583
Listen, you'll find me very
appreciative when you get here.

299
00:10:09,583 --> 00:10:11,492
- I saved you half a can of Pringles.

300
00:10:11,492 --> 00:10:13,525
- Okay, bye, bye.

301
00:10:13,525 --> 00:10:16,079
- That's so understanding.

302
00:10:16,079 --> 00:10:17,242
- [Tom Servo] How about this, beep.

303
00:10:17,242 --> 00:10:20,015
Can you here this, beep.

304
00:10:20,015 --> 00:10:22,267
(car stereo playing)
- Well, here we are.

305
00:10:22,267 --> 00:10:24,963
- [Crow] The Joe Don Baker Museum.

306
00:10:24,963 --> 00:10:27,894
- You've got to be kidding!

307
00:10:27,894 --> 00:10:29,126
- You said park.

308
00:10:29,126 --> 00:10:31,589
- [Crow] Crank up the Molly
Hatchet and go to town.

309
00:10:31,589 --> 00:10:34,672
- [Tom Servo] I like you Dotty, like!

310
00:10:36,760 --> 00:10:38,449
- Can you come again tomorrow night?

311
00:10:38,449 --> 00:10:40,149
- Well I certainly hope so.

312
00:10:40,149 --> 00:10:41,928
- The revival will be still here.

313
00:10:41,928 --> 00:10:43,850
- Give me that old time religion.

314
00:10:43,850 --> 00:10:44,683
- [Crow] (groans)

315
00:10:44,683 --> 00:10:48,125
Boy, I can hardly wait to get
saved again tomorrow night.

316
00:10:48,125 --> 00:10:49,490
- Oh Dan, wait.

317
00:10:49,490 --> 00:10:51,988
- [Tom Servo] I forgot
to validate your parking.

318
00:10:51,988 --> 00:10:53,244
- You forgot your back brace.

319
00:10:53,244 --> 00:10:54,431
- [Mike, Tom Servo,
Crow] (groan disgustedly)

320
00:10:54,431 --> 00:10:55,522
- [Mike] Oh my.

321
00:10:55,522 --> 00:10:56,480
- Keesh.

322
00:10:56,480 --> 00:10:57,775
- [Mike] Oh, he's pink.

323
00:10:57,775 --> 00:10:59,994
- [Tom Servo] I don't know
how, but I just became sterile.

324
00:10:59,994 --> 00:11:03,710
- Go spiders, go spiders, go, go spiders!

325
00:11:03,710 --> 00:11:06,917
- I saw a star fall from
heaven unto the Earth,

326
00:11:06,917 --> 00:11:09,735
and there arose a smoke out of the pit

327
00:11:09,735 --> 00:11:11,734
as a smoke from a great furnace.

328
00:11:11,734 --> 00:11:13,516
- [Mike] Then add the ribs and cook.

329
00:11:13,516 --> 00:11:15,975
- And out of the smoke there
came locusts upon the Earth

330
00:11:15,975 --> 00:11:18,849
and unto them was given power.

331
00:11:18,849 --> 00:11:21,192
- [Tom Servo] Can I
just get my Tupperware?

332
00:11:21,192 --> 00:11:23,859
- [Crow] Pull up Laika, pull up!

333
00:11:24,741 --> 00:11:27,887
♫ I love tick infested hounds

334
00:11:27,887 --> 00:11:29,854
♫ Slaughterin' a deer

335
00:11:29,854 --> 00:11:32,361
♫ and beer ♫

336
00:11:32,361 --> 00:11:35,528
- [Tom Servo] Ah, Brett Favre at home.

337
00:11:36,923 --> 00:11:39,861
- [Mike] Now they're poor
only in money and spirit

338
00:11:39,861 --> 00:11:43,194
and dignity and moral fiber and hygiene.

339
00:11:44,297 --> 00:11:46,047
- [Tom Servo] Hi hud.

340
00:11:47,734 --> 00:11:48,897
- How was it?

341
00:11:48,897 --> 00:11:50,580
- [Tom Servo] How was
your day at the whore?

342
00:11:50,580 --> 00:11:51,413
- Great.

343
00:11:51,413 --> 00:11:52,246
- [Tom Servo] R-r-r-ribbit!

344
00:11:52,246 --> 00:11:54,579
- So what did the preacher talk about?

345
00:11:54,579 --> 00:11:55,975
- Sin.

346
00:11:55,975 --> 00:11:57,173
- Like a rock!

347
00:11:57,173 --> 00:11:58,644
- What did he have to say about it?

348
00:11:58,644 --> 00:12:01,383
- He, uh, was against it.

349
00:12:01,383 --> 00:12:02,972
- Listen dammit,

350
00:12:02,972 --> 00:12:04,957
- [Tom Servo] Can we get the
boom mic a little closer?

351
00:12:04,957 --> 00:12:06,452
- [Mike] The movie that
takes the bold step

352
00:12:06,452 --> 00:12:09,271
of not including the audience.

353
00:12:09,271 --> 00:12:10,521
- Look at that.

354
00:12:13,868 --> 00:12:17,373
- [Tom Servo] Blaze area,
with music by Pink Floyd.

355
00:12:17,373 --> 00:12:18,847
- Hooterville was decimated

356
00:12:18,847 --> 00:12:21,226
by scud missiles that day.

357
00:12:21,226 --> 00:12:23,288
- What the hell was that?

358
00:12:23,288 --> 00:12:24,121
- Weird.

359
00:12:24,990 --> 00:12:28,274
Jeez, would you listen to that wind?

360
00:12:28,274 --> 00:12:30,750
- [Tom Servo] Meanwhile, a
woman needs a light wrap.

361
00:12:30,750 --> 00:12:33,686
(Crow snickers)

362
00:12:33,686 --> 00:12:35,180
- Lights are dead.

363
00:12:35,180 --> 00:12:36,236
- What's wrong?

364
00:12:36,236 --> 00:12:37,425
- [Tom Servo] They could
rub their keana together

365
00:12:37,425 --> 00:12:39,209
and create static to keep
warm if they're cold.

366
00:12:39,209 --> 00:12:41,410
- [Mike] (Laughs) Yeah.

367
00:12:41,410 --> 00:12:42,704
- Car won't start either.

368
00:12:42,704 --> 00:12:44,183
- [Mike] And my skin is getting waxy.

369
00:12:44,183 --> 00:12:45,252
- [Terry] Great!

370
00:12:45,252 --> 00:12:46,292
- Wait here Terry.

371
00:12:46,292 --> 00:12:49,007
- [Crow] I'll turn off the wind machine.

372
00:12:49,007 --> 00:12:52,007
- [Tom Servo] It's the new 1971 car!

373
00:12:53,283 --> 00:12:55,100
- [Mike] Well the air filter is fine.

374
00:12:55,100 --> 00:12:57,158
- [Terry] Hey, come on!

375
00:12:57,158 --> 00:12:58,455
- I figured we could have sex

376
00:12:58,455 --> 00:13:03,265
'till this blows over!
(laughing)

377
00:13:03,265 --> 00:13:05,932
- [Tom Servo] Auber camoo, safe!

378
00:13:09,994 --> 00:13:11,911
- Moses, move the bike!

379
00:13:15,648 --> 00:13:17,144
- [Tom Servo] Boy, I hope
that bomb didn't land

380
00:13:17,144 --> 00:13:19,143
on our pile of tires and
our busted refrigerator

381
00:13:19,143 --> 00:13:23,310
in the yard, and the rusted
chassis of our '68 Impala.

382
00:13:25,163 --> 00:13:27,807
- What the hell was that?

383
00:13:27,807 --> 00:13:31,358
- [Tom Servo] It's befuddling
my dumb cracker mind.

384
00:13:31,358 --> 00:13:33,025
- Steve Prefontaine.

385
00:13:34,242 --> 00:13:37,553
- [Tom Servo] Satan is out running.

386
00:13:37,553 --> 00:13:38,553
Normal Foot!

387
00:13:40,117 --> 00:13:40,961
- [Mike] Big foot.

388
00:13:40,961 --> 00:13:42,044
- [Ev] It was a shooting star.

389
00:13:42,044 --> 00:13:43,326
- Like a rock!

390
00:13:43,326 --> 00:13:44,890
- [Mike] Okay, like them, a little much.

391
00:13:44,890 --> 00:13:47,279
- [Dan] There's nothing there now.

392
00:13:47,279 --> 00:13:51,196
No fire, no smoke, no
smell, no sound, nothing.

393
00:13:52,702 --> 00:13:54,082
- [Ev] You saw it, too?

394
00:13:54,082 --> 00:13:55,245
It wasn't just me.

395
00:13:55,245 --> 00:13:56,508
You saw it.

396
00:13:56,508 --> 00:13:58,091
There must be something out there.

397
00:13:58,091 --> 00:13:59,215
- [Tom Servo] Of course,
we are dumb cheeseheads.

398
00:13:59,215 --> 00:14:01,704
- Well, whatever it is,
it can keep 'till morning.

399
00:14:01,704 --> 00:14:03,277
- [Tom Servo] I'll leave
a light on for you.

400
00:14:03,277 --> 00:14:05,506
- You mean to say that
all hell just busted loose

401
00:14:05,506 --> 00:14:08,384
in our field and you're going on into bed?

402
00:14:08,384 --> 00:14:09,498
- [Dan] I'm tired.

403
00:14:09,498 --> 00:14:10,680
- And repulsive and stupid.

404
00:14:10,680 --> 00:14:12,816
- You're always tired.

405
00:14:12,816 --> 00:14:16,429
- Well that revival
really took it out of me.

406
00:14:16,429 --> 00:14:18,533
Now if you want to, you
can stay out here all night

407
00:14:18,533 --> 00:14:20,082
looking at nothing.

408
00:14:20,082 --> 00:14:22,123
- [Tom Servo] This isn't a
very good remake of Sabrina.

409
00:14:22,123 --> 00:14:25,313
- Packers fans, the horrible truth.

410
00:14:25,313 --> 00:14:27,319
- [Tom Servo] Flush.

411
00:14:27,319 --> 00:14:31,023
♫ It's the good life ♫

412
00:14:31,023 --> 00:14:33,356
(pop music)

413
00:14:40,791 --> 00:14:42,625
(buzzer)

414
00:14:42,625 --> 00:14:46,042
- [Crow] America Online tries to keep up.

415
00:14:46,938 --> 00:14:51,062
- [Tom Servo] Red phones are
hot in Paris this spring.

416
00:14:51,062 --> 00:14:52,691
- [Mike] He's got a copy of Varmint Master

417
00:14:52,691 --> 00:14:53,762
hidden inside that.

418
00:14:53,762 --> 00:14:55,781
(Crow snickers)

419
00:14:55,781 --> 00:14:56,993
- Hello.

420
00:14:56,993 --> 00:14:58,756
Sheriff's Office.

421
00:14:58,756 --> 00:15:00,176
- Don't act with your tongue, Alan.

422
00:15:00,176 --> 00:15:01,009
- I see.

423
00:15:01,009 --> 00:15:02,726
- [Tom Servo] I should button my shirt.

424
00:15:02,726 --> 00:15:04,736
- So your radio won't work?

425
00:15:04,736 --> 00:15:08,099
Well all I can tell you
is call Joe's Radio Shop.

426
00:15:08,099 --> 00:15:09,786
He opens 9am sharp.

427
00:15:09,786 --> 00:15:10,837
- [Mike] So your space based

428
00:15:10,837 --> 00:15:12,587
missile defense system won't work?

429
00:15:12,587 --> 00:15:13,784
- Your car won't start?

430
00:15:13,784 --> 00:15:14,877
- Then you might be a redneck.

431
00:15:14,877 --> 00:15:17,572
- All I can tell you is
call Ernie's Auto Repair.

432
00:15:17,572 --> 00:15:18,960
He opens at eight.

433
00:15:18,960 --> 00:15:21,540
- [Mike] Maybe he's Amish and
doesn't believe in buttons.

434
00:15:21,540 --> 00:15:23,037
- No ma'am, I don't have the number.

435
00:15:23,037 --> 00:15:24,315
- [Tom Servo] Take your time movie.

436
00:15:24,315 --> 00:15:27,507
- All I can tell you is
use the yellow pages.

437
00:15:27,507 --> 00:15:29,868
Let your fingers do
the walking. (laughing)

438
00:15:29,868 --> 00:15:31,761
- Not a joke but an incredible simulation.

439
00:15:31,761 --> 00:15:33,271
(dial tone sounding)

440
00:15:33,271 --> 00:15:34,137
- That's funny.

441
00:15:34,137 --> 00:15:35,705
I wonder why she hung up on me.

442
00:15:35,705 --> 00:15:40,502
- [Mike] Maybe your bodily funk
travels over the phone line.

443
00:15:40,502 --> 00:15:41,346
- [Tom Servo] Actually filmed

444
00:15:41,346 --> 00:15:44,679
inside the thumb hole of a bowling ball.

445
00:15:45,513 --> 00:15:47,013
- Film extra noir.

446
00:15:48,373 --> 00:15:49,206
- [Mike] Hello?

447
00:15:49,206 --> 00:15:50,914
Movie, come on movie, come here boy.

448
00:15:50,914 --> 00:15:52,313
(whistling)

449
00:15:52,313 --> 00:15:53,807
- Don't move or I'll shoot!

450
00:15:53,807 --> 00:15:55,009
- [Tom Servo] Don't turn on the light!

451
00:15:55,009 --> 00:15:57,881
No!
- [Crow] (groans)

452
00:15:57,881 --> 00:15:59,222
- That scared the death out of me.

453
00:15:59,222 --> 00:16:00,963
- Aw, he's lactating.

454
00:16:00,963 --> 00:16:02,211
- Put the gun away.

455
00:16:02,211 --> 00:16:05,013
- What the hell are you doing
sneaking in here at this hour?

456
00:16:05,013 --> 00:16:06,422
- [Mike] What a handsome man.

457
00:16:06,422 --> 00:16:07,998
- Had to walk home.

458
00:16:07,998 --> 00:16:10,319
- [Tom Servo] Young Bill and
Hillary struggle to make it.

459
00:16:10,319 --> 00:16:13,393
- I warned ya, that little
parking spot is rotten.

460
00:16:13,393 --> 00:16:14,721
- Want a piece of milk?

461
00:16:14,721 --> 00:16:17,012
- It wasn't Dave's fault,
his car broke down.

462
00:16:17,012 --> 00:16:18,768
- [Tom Servo] Hey, would
you call this food?

463
00:16:18,768 --> 00:16:20,731
- (laughs) You fell for that old trick.

464
00:16:20,731 --> 00:16:23,254
- [Tom Servo] Oh Magoo,
you've done it again.

465
00:16:23,254 --> 00:16:25,951
- That had whiskers on
it when I was a kid.

466
00:16:25,951 --> 00:16:28,272
- It really did break down.

467
00:16:28,272 --> 00:16:30,220
- Yeah, where?

468
00:16:30,220 --> 00:16:31,696
- In the junkyard.

469
00:16:31,696 --> 00:16:33,778
- Must be like a homecoming
for you, eh Mike?

470
00:16:33,778 --> 00:16:36,202
- That's exactly where a
horny little punk like that

471
00:16:36,202 --> 00:16:37,738
would park, in a junkyard.

472
00:16:37,738 --> 00:16:39,343
- [Tom Servo] Our proud Viking heritage.

473
00:16:39,343 --> 00:16:42,853
- I hate to burst your
bubble, but it was my idea.

474
00:16:42,853 --> 00:16:45,728
- I ought to put you over my knee,

475
00:16:45,728 --> 00:16:48,437
pull down your britches and
spank the hell out of ya!

476
00:16:48,437 --> 00:16:51,754
- Oh, I always wondered why
you used to spank me so much.

477
00:16:51,754 --> 00:16:53,480
You could get your jollies.

478
00:16:53,480 --> 00:16:54,733
(banjo music)

479
00:16:54,733 --> 00:16:57,758
- (Mike) And the movie
ramps up the repulsion.

480
00:16:57,758 --> 00:17:00,486
- This movie hates us, doesn't it?

481
00:17:00,486 --> 00:17:03,862
- [Tom Servo] Well I better
finish my silverfish en croute.

482
00:17:03,862 --> 00:17:06,262
- Man can't even have any
peace in his own house.

483
00:17:06,262 --> 00:17:09,595
- [Mike] Well, Section 8 owns the house.

484
00:17:10,939 --> 00:17:13,192
- A showered person, thank God!

485
00:17:13,192 --> 00:17:14,503
- [Mike] Guys, it's Della Street.

486
00:17:14,503 --> 00:17:17,503
- [Tom Servo] Whoa!
- [Crow] Oh yeah.

487
00:17:18,341 --> 00:17:21,298
- [Mike] It’s the hotline
to Paul’s operatives.

488
00:17:21,298 --> 00:17:23,453
- Mr. Kester, all your tests are positive.

489
00:17:23,453 --> 00:17:26,576
- Yes, this is Dr. Langer from
Montclaire Observatory again.

490
00:17:26,576 --> 00:17:27,909
I've got a gamma-ray shower

491
00:17:27,909 --> 00:17:29,125
and the barometer has dropped an inch

492
00:17:29,125 --> 00:17:30,235
in less than 20 minutes.

493
00:17:30,235 --> 00:17:31,732
- [Tom Servo] Should I
wear shorts or slacks?

494
00:17:31,732 --> 00:17:34,380
- That's unprecedented, right, right.

495
00:17:34,380 --> 00:17:36,578
And none of the other
phenomena I'm recording

496
00:17:36,578 --> 00:17:40,036
correlate with any previously
observed data in this area.

497
00:17:40,036 --> 00:17:43,985
- [Mike] So I thought we
should cut to Cape Canaveral.

498
00:17:43,985 --> 00:17:45,809
- [Tom Servo] The story
of regional planning.

499
00:17:45,809 --> 00:17:49,976
Careful zoning regulation,
rational development controls.

500
00:17:52,566 --> 00:17:54,649
- The philodendron story!

501
00:17:56,975 --> 00:17:59,539
- [Mike] Polish toilet paper
dispenser, that's great.

502
00:17:59,539 --> 00:18:00,622
I gotta put that up.

503
00:18:00,622 --> 00:18:03,530
- Did I ever tell you, you're gorgeous?

504
00:18:03,530 --> 00:18:04,991
