1009
00:35:48,500 --> 00:35:49,333
- That's right.

1010
00:35:49,333 --> 00:35:51,009
- They're supposed to,
but they're too damn lazy.

1011
00:35:51,009 --> 00:35:52,177
- [Mike] You see, he remembers that

1012
00:35:52,177 --> 00:35:54,556
from his last year of school in 3rd grade.

1013
00:35:54,556 --> 00:35:55,567
- [Tom Servo] Too bad their windows

1014
00:35:55,567 --> 00:35:58,679
are made from cellophane and duct-tape.

1015
00:35:58,679 --> 00:36:00,429
- Aryan Nation rules.

1016
00:36:05,185 --> 00:36:06,018
- Look at that.

1017
00:36:06,018 --> 00:36:08,013
- [Mike] I made a R.

1018
00:36:08,013 --> 00:36:09,061
- [Tom Servo] (humming
Gilligan’s Island theme)

1019
00:36:09,061 --> 00:36:10,752
- [Voiceover] Hello?

1020
00:36:10,752 --> 00:36:12,426
- Hi Dr. Langer.

1021
00:36:12,426 --> 00:36:13,408
How are you this morning?

1022
00:36:13,408 --> 00:36:14,846
Would you join me please?

1023
00:36:14,846 --> 00:36:15,882
- Round o' bacon!

1024
00:36:15,882 --> 00:36:16,799
I'm buying.

1025
00:36:18,228 --> 00:36:20,246
- This your brother from Ascot?

1026
00:36:20,246 --> 00:36:22,896
- No this is Dr. Vance from NASA.

1027
00:36:22,896 --> 00:36:23,976
- Hello Sheriff.

1028
00:36:23,976 --> 00:36:26,389
- NASA, National Aeronautics
and Space Administration,

1029
00:36:26,389 --> 00:36:27,222
that NASAU?

1030
00:36:27,222 --> 00:36:28,496
- [Tom Servo] No, Long Island.

1031
00:36:28,496 --> 00:36:30,976
- Yes, but it's NASA.

1032
00:36:30,976 --> 00:36:32,353
Houston, Texas.

1033
00:36:32,353 --> 00:36:34,179
- Sheriff, we have to talk to you

1034
00:36:34,179 --> 00:36:36,280
about last night's disturbances.

1035
00:36:36,280 --> 00:36:37,283
- Say no more.

1036
00:36:37,283 --> 00:36:39,499
I'll get that preacher man
to tone it down tonight.

1037
00:36:39,499 --> 00:36:41,983
- No, no, I don't mean that disturbance.

1038
00:36:41,983 --> 00:36:42,816
- Oh, no?

1039
00:36:43,941 --> 00:36:45,303
Pardon me Doctor.

1040
00:36:45,303 --> 00:36:46,906
- [Mike] There's a crumb
I didn't eat there.

1041
00:36:46,906 --> 00:36:48,802
- One of our local spiders. (laughs)

1042
00:36:48,802 --> 00:36:51,580
- So it's stupid and smells of beer sweat?

1043
00:36:51,580 --> 00:36:52,785
- Hey what's that gizmo?

1044
00:36:52,785 --> 00:36:54,112
- [Tom Servo] It's my pacemaker.

1045
00:36:54,112 --> 00:36:56,320
- It's a Geiger counter.

1046
00:36:56,320 --> 00:36:57,385
- A Geiger counter!

1047
00:36:57,385 --> 00:36:59,389
Well we don't have any
Geigers around here.

1048
00:36:59,389 --> 00:37:00,958
Never did have in these parts.

1049
00:37:00,958 --> 00:37:02,142
- [Mike] (laughs sarcastically) Kill him.

1050
00:37:02,142 --> 00:37:04,335
- No Sheriff you misunderstand me.

1051
00:37:04,335 --> 00:37:07,888
See, Dr. Geiger invented
this to count the nuclear--

1052
00:37:07,888 --> 00:37:10,097
- Oh Vance, Vance, I have
a feeling the Sheriff

1053
00:37:10,097 --> 00:37:11,379
is putting you on.

1054
00:37:11,379 --> 00:37:13,117
I'm sure he's taken physics.

1055
00:37:13,117 --> 00:37:16,207
- Oh I used to take physics,
but now I find that--

1056
00:37:16,207 --> 00:37:17,534
- Uh, joke coming in!

1057
00:37:17,534 --> 00:37:19,228
- prunes do the better job for me.

1058
00:37:19,228 --> 00:37:22,145
- (painful groans)

1059
00:37:23,296 --> 00:37:24,814
- We're going to be rich.

1060
00:37:24,814 --> 00:37:26,129
- What do you mean we?

1061
00:37:26,129 --> 00:37:27,502
- [Tom Servo] You, me and booze.

1062
00:37:27,502 --> 00:37:28,977
- This farm is mine.

1063
00:37:28,977 --> 00:37:31,604
Everything that's on it is mine.

1064
00:37:31,604 --> 00:37:33,812
- [Mike] Every dead cow.

1065
00:37:33,812 --> 00:37:36,816
- Nobody ever found
diamonds around here before.

1066
00:37:36,816 --> 00:37:37,966
I think they came out of that

1067
00:37:37,966 --> 00:37:39,655
weird fireball thing last night.

1068
00:37:39,655 --> 00:37:41,303
- (burping and farting sounds)

1069
00:37:41,303 --> 00:37:43,328
- Take these into cousin
Billy at the Rock Shop.

1070
00:37:43,328 --> 00:37:44,161
- [Tom Servo] Billy!

1071
00:37:44,161 --> 00:37:46,655
- He can tell me just
exactly what they're worth.

1072
00:37:46,655 --> 00:37:49,469
- But don't you tell cousin
Billy where you found them.

1073
00:37:49,469 --> 00:37:51,009
That'll be our secret.

1074
00:37:51,009 --> 00:37:52,710
- [Tom Servo] Alvino, honey, I love you.

1075
00:37:52,710 --> 00:37:54,361
- Don't look at me like that Dan,

1076
00:37:54,361 --> 00:37:55,829
you and me are going to be rich.

1077
00:37:55,829 --> 00:37:57,753
- [Mike] Think of the toilet you can buy.

1078
00:37:57,753 --> 00:37:59,242
- Dan that's not fair.

1079
00:37:59,242 --> 00:38:00,923
I never meant any of those nasty things

1080
00:38:00,923 --> 00:38:02,181
I used to say to you.

1081
00:38:02,181 --> 00:38:03,764
I was just teasing.

1082
00:38:04,633 --> 00:38:06,030
- I'm going to call off this invasion.

1083
00:38:06,030 --> 00:38:08,697
This place is just not worth it.

1084
00:38:11,490 --> 00:38:14,278
- [Tom Servo] (burps) It’s them
welfare moms sucking us dry.

1085
00:38:14,278 --> 00:38:15,980
- [Dave] Hi Dr. Langer,
good morning Sheriff.

1086
00:38:15,980 --> 00:38:16,938
- [Sheriff] Morning.
- [Dr. Langer] Hello dear.

1087
00:38:16,938 --> 00:38:17,771
- [Dave] May I join you?

1088
00:38:17,771 --> 00:38:18,604
- Please.

1089
00:38:18,604 --> 00:38:19,437
- Thank you.

1090
00:38:19,437 --> 00:38:22,021
- This is Dave Perkins, his
father runs the local newspaper.

1091
00:38:22,021 --> 00:38:23,025
- [Crow] He’s Mrs. Pynchon.

1092
00:38:23,025 --> 00:38:24,225
- Hello Dave, nice to see you.

1093
00:38:24,225 --> 00:38:25,416
- Dr. Vance from NASA.

1094
00:38:25,416 --> 00:38:26,749
- NASA huh?

1095
00:38:26,749 --> 00:38:28,459
- NASA, Houston.

1096
00:38:28,459 --> 00:38:29,848
- [Mike] Where they have a problem.

1097
00:38:29,848 --> 00:38:30,681
- What brings you here?

1098
00:38:30,681 --> 00:38:32,504
Anything I can publish in the paper?

1099
00:38:32,504 --> 00:38:34,015
- That's classified.

1100
00:38:34,015 --> 00:38:35,760
- Well, I'll put it in
the Classified section.

1101
00:38:35,760 --> 00:38:37,720
- (laughs) Well that's safe enough.

1102
00:38:37,720 --> 00:38:39,222
Nobody reads your ads anyway.

1103
00:38:39,222 --> 00:38:40,954
- [Tom Servo] The fun Sheriff.

1104
00:38:40,954 --> 00:38:43,500
- Uh, Dave, could I speak
to you for a moment?

1105
00:38:43,500 --> 00:38:44,704
- [Dave] Sure Dr. Vance.

1106
00:38:44,704 --> 00:38:45,959
- But no touching.

1107
00:38:45,959 --> 00:38:47,484
- Excuse us a moment.

1108
00:38:47,484 --> 00:38:49,673
- [Mike] Now, do you recommend
the chicken fried steak

1109
00:38:49,673 --> 00:38:51,506
or the walleye cheeks?

1110
00:38:52,947 --> 00:38:54,553
- Pudding!

1111
00:38:54,553 --> 00:38:56,230
- [Tom Servo] Yeah, you
can borrow my shirt.

1112
00:38:56,230 --> 00:38:57,976
- Is he always that serious?

1113
00:38:57,976 --> 00:39:01,059
- Well, he has something to
be serious about at this time.

1114
00:39:01,059 --> 00:39:02,142
- You know, I wonder if

1115
00:39:02,142 --> 00:39:03,632
what happened to Terry and I last night

1116
00:39:03,632 --> 00:39:05,968
had something to do with
what you're talking about.

1117
00:39:05,968 --> 00:39:06,801
- What?

1118
00:39:06,801 --> 00:39:08,272
- What happened to you and Terry?

1119
00:39:08,272 --> 00:39:09,210
- First base, woo!

1120
00:39:09,210 --> 00:39:10,511
- Well we were parked by the junkyard.

1121
00:39:10,511 --> 00:39:12,255
The lights went, they went dead,

1122
00:39:12,255 --> 00:39:14,527
the radio wouldn't work and
the engine wouldn't start.

1123
00:39:14,527 --> 00:39:16,716
A wind came up and started, I don't know,

1124
00:39:16,716 --> 00:39:18,238
everything just went wrong.

1125
00:39:18,238 --> 00:39:19,303
- [Tom Servo] Thoughtful or hungry?

1126
00:39:19,303 --> 00:39:20,786
You decide.

1127
00:39:20,786 --> 00:39:22,015
- [Mike] Hour three of the invasion.

1128
00:39:22,015 --> 00:39:23,987
We took the refrigerator.

1129
00:39:23,987 --> 00:39:28,377
- Thanks for breakfast
ma'am, I'll clean up.

1130
00:39:28,377 --> 00:39:29,869
- [Mike] The doctor should
have been more specific

1131
00:39:29,869 --> 00:39:33,286
when he told her to get plenty of fluids.

1132
00:39:35,181 --> 00:39:37,004
(dog whimpering sound)

1133
00:39:37,004 --> 00:39:39,346
- [Mike] Honey, I need changing again.

1134
00:39:39,346 --> 00:39:42,110
- You're hitting the booze again, huh?

1135
00:39:42,110 --> 00:39:44,456
- Leave me alone I feel terrible.

1136
00:39:44,456 --> 00:39:47,509
This place is full of spiders.

1137
00:39:47,509 --> 00:39:50,639
- Yeah, I know, little pink ones.

1138
00:39:50,639 --> 00:39:54,644
- No, no, big, big, black
hairy ones, with furry legs.

1139
00:39:54,644 --> 00:39:55,690
- No that's me.

1140
00:39:55,690 --> 00:39:56,523
- Uh huh.

1141
00:39:56,523 --> 00:39:59,453
Lay off the booze Ev, and they'll go away.

1142
00:39:59,453 --> 00:40:01,258
- [Mike] You know, in her
defense, laying off the booze

1143
00:40:01,258 --> 00:40:03,267
would mean seeing him sober.

1144
00:40:03,267 --> 00:40:05,100
- That's true.

1145
00:40:05,100 --> 00:40:07,517
(telephone ringing)

1146
00:40:07,517 --> 00:40:09,799
- [Mike] Doughy has-been.

1147
00:40:09,799 --> 00:40:11,950
- Hello, Sheriff's Office.

1148
00:40:11,950 --> 00:40:13,738
Oh, yes Mrs. Cooper, how are you?

1149
00:40:13,738 --> 00:40:14,571
- [Tom Servo] Pancakes?

1150
00:40:14,571 --> 00:40:16,533
I'll be right over.

1151
00:40:16,533 --> 00:40:17,366
- Missing?

1152
00:40:17,366 --> 00:40:18,612
- Well where are you?

1153
00:40:18,612 --> 00:40:20,757
Well take a good look around
and that's where you would be.

1154
00:40:20,757 --> 00:40:21,968
- When did you see him last?

1155
00:40:21,968 --> 00:40:23,689
- [Mike] 1953?

1156
00:40:23,689 --> 00:40:26,209
- You haven't seen him since last night?

1157
00:40:26,209 --> 00:40:29,062
We'll I'd be glad to drive
out and take a look for him.

1158
00:40:29,062 --> 00:40:30,693
What color is his motorcycle?

1159
00:40:30,693 --> 00:40:32,071
- [Tom Servo] Personally,
I've never been able to

1160
00:40:32,071 --> 00:40:33,336
start seeing motorcycles.

1161
00:40:33,336 --> 00:40:34,917
- Come on dear, please, stop worrying.

1162
00:40:34,917 --> 00:40:36,482
I'm sure he'll turn up safe and sound.

1163
00:40:36,482 --> 00:40:38,684
I'll be there after my pre-lunch snack.

1164
00:40:38,684 --> 00:40:41,518
- Yes, I'll get in touch with you.

1165
00:40:41,518 --> 00:40:42,435
Right, bye.

1166
00:40:44,338 --> 00:40:47,755
(instrumental pop music)

1167
00:40:53,221 --> 00:40:55,473
- Boy, how come you only get tired

1168
00:40:55,473 --> 00:40:56,722
when you have to stay awake

1169
00:40:56,722 --> 00:41:00,784
to avoid being replaced by an
evil pod creature, huh Servo?

1170
00:41:00,784 --> 00:41:01,617
Servo!

1171
00:41:01,617 --> 00:41:04,092
- Yarg! I am awake Mike, I can stay awake.

1172
00:41:04,092 --> 00:41:06,242
I just need a little shut eye.

1173
00:41:06,242 --> 00:41:07,075
- No!

1174
00:41:07,075 --> 00:41:08,847
No no no no, don't pass out on me now.

1175
00:41:08,847 --> 00:41:10,956
We have to stay awake
to avoid being replaced

1176
00:41:10,956 --> 00:41:14,430
by a pod creature from
Gypsy's evil doppelganger.

1177
00:41:14,430 --> 00:41:16,789
- Ah, please Mike, doo-pel-uh-gen-gur.

1178
00:41:16,789 --> 00:41:19,459
I'm of the umlaut, Doopleginger.

1179
00:41:19,459 --> 00:41:21,496
- Doopleging, doopleging.

1180
00:41:21,496 --> 00:41:23,177
- Round the lips.

1181
00:41:23,177 --> 00:41:25,119
- I'll round your lips now, Crow.

1182
00:41:25,119 --> 00:41:26,791
- I'm fine, I'm fine ah Mike.

1183
00:41:26,791 --> 00:41:29,489
A French roast, a
v-v-Vivarin, uh diet pills,

1184
00:41:29,489 --> 00:41:31,870
Mountain Dew, Jolt, Watered Joes,

1185
00:41:31,870 --> 00:41:34,388
Surge, chocolate covered espresso beans,

1186
00:41:34,388 --> 00:41:36,572
M & M's and I'm listening to Nitzer Ebb

1187
00:41:36,572 --> 00:41:38,871
and I'm fine Mike, really I'm fine.

1188
00:41:38,871 --> 00:41:39,704
- Alright, Okay.

1189
00:41:39,704 --> 00:41:41,644
Just don't uh, don't explode,

1190
00:41:41,644 --> 00:41:43,682
I'm going to check in on the planet here.

1191
00:41:43,682 --> 00:41:47,793
- (groaning) Oh, hi Nelson.

1192
00:41:47,793 --> 00:41:50,299
Just getting the last of these ticks off.

1193
00:41:50,299 --> 00:41:51,947
- Bobo, is that you?

1194
00:41:51,947 --> 00:41:53,447
I mean really you?

1195
00:41:55,023 --> 00:41:56,780
- No, It's John Shuck on a bad hair day.

1196
00:41:56,780 --> 00:41:58,182
Of course it's me!

1197
00:41:58,182 --> 00:42:01,158
And I'm fine, but these two, hoo hoo hoo,

1198
00:42:01,158 --> 00:42:03,142
they really love their zucchinis.

1199
00:42:03,142 --> 00:42:04,785
In fact they're packing them up

1200
00:42:04,785 --> 00:42:06,312
so that they can deliver zucchinis

1201
00:42:06,312 --> 00:42:08,938
to their friends all over the galaxy.

1202
00:42:08,938 --> 00:42:11,041
- Now, listen very carefully Bobo,

1203
00:42:11,041 --> 00:42:14,354
those pods grow aliens
who replace your body.

1204
00:42:14,354 --> 00:42:15,779
If they're loading them into the truck

1205
00:42:15,779 --> 00:42:19,593
that means the whole
galaxy could be in danger.

1206
00:42:19,593 --> 00:42:21,320
- Oh come now.

1207
00:42:21,320 --> 00:42:23,922
Just because they load a bunch
of zucchini throw pillows

1208
00:42:23,922 --> 00:42:25,760
onto a truck doesn't mean they're trying

1209
00:42:25,760 --> 00:42:28,086
to take over the galaxy.

1210
00:42:28,086 --> 00:42:28,997
Preposterous.

1211
00:42:28,997 --> 00:42:31,076
Typical of you with your back

1212
00:42:31,076 --> 00:42:33,816
and your bra and hand blenders.

1213
00:42:33,816 --> 00:42:35,271
Look, I'll just ask her.

1214
00:42:35,271 --> 00:42:38,433
Oh say, law giver, now are those evil pods

1215
00:42:38,433 --> 00:42:41,611
and are you trying to
take over the galaxy?

1216
00:42:41,611 --> 00:42:43,484
- Yes and yes.

1217
00:42:43,484 --> 00:42:45,148
Excuse me please.

1218
00:42:45,148 --> 00:42:45,981
- Oh.

1219
00:42:47,898 --> 00:42:49,534
Well I guess I can see

1220
00:42:49,534 --> 00:42:51,468
how you could misconstrue that Nelson,

1221
00:42:51,468 --> 00:42:53,705
but I'm still not convinced.

1222
00:42:53,705 --> 00:42:55,839
- What do you mean you don't?

1223
00:42:55,839 --> 00:42:58,094
Look, calm down, look just do me a favor

1224
00:42:58,094 --> 00:43:01,038
and try taking one of those
pods off the truck, okay?

1225
00:43:01,038 --> 00:43:03,799
- Alright, I'll humor you.

1226
00:43:03,799 --> 00:43:08,079
Let me see if I can grab
one of these babies here,

1227
00:43:08,079 --> 00:43:09,079
there we go.

1228
00:43:15,034 --> 00:43:19,201
I don't remember taking
another one of those with me.

1229
00:43:20,178 --> 00:43:22,554
Well now this is odd.

1230
00:43:22,554 --> 00:43:26,018
And she did say she wanted to
take over the galaxy and...

1231
00:43:26,018 --> 00:43:28,831
- (screeches)

1232
00:43:28,831 --> 00:43:32,252
- Nelson, I see your point,
you may be onto something.

1233
00:43:32,252 --> 00:43:35,505
The universe is in danger
but don't you worry,

1234
00:43:35,505 --> 00:43:38,310
No sirree Bob, I'm on the job!

1235
00:43:38,310 --> 00:43:39,897
I'll stop these two wretched creatures

1236
00:43:39,897 --> 00:43:41,245
and foil their little plan.

1237
00:43:41,245 --> 00:43:44,959
(muffled speaking)

1238
00:43:44,959 --> 00:43:49,292
(heart beating)
- Well again, we're doomed.

1239
00:43:49,292 --> 00:43:50,743
- What's that horrible thumping?

1240
00:43:50,743 --> 00:43:54,531
It's my heart, I think I'm, I think I'm,

1241
00:43:54,531 --> 00:43:56,489
- He's going to blow!

1242
00:43:56,489 --> 00:43:59,775
(warning buzzer sounding)
- It's movie time!

1243
00:43:59,775 --> 00:44:00,980
(bang)

1244
00:44:00,980 --> 00:44:02,792
(mechanical whirring)

1245
00:44:02,792 --> 00:44:04,709
(thud)

1246
00:44:06,021 --> 00:44:07,691
(beeping)

1247
00:44:07,691 --> 00:44:10,279
(metal creaking)

1248
00:44:10,279 --> 00:44:11,793
- Hurry up, hurry up you guys!

1249
00:44:11,793 --> 00:44:12,626
Please.

1250
00:44:15,251 --> 00:44:17,923
- [Mike] Alas, poor Yorick, woo-hee!

1251
00:44:17,923 --> 00:44:19,498
- I'm gonna pre-bury myself

1252
00:44:19,498 --> 00:44:21,970
to save time after I die.

1253
00:44:21,970 --> 00:44:25,530
(crazy laughing)

1254
00:44:25,530 --> 00:44:28,593
- He's a freelance Pooper Scooper.

1255
00:44:28,593 --> 00:44:32,512
- [Mike] They whacked the Crypt Keeper.

1256
00:44:32,512 --> 00:44:36,043
- Whatever it is, it's
drizzled with chocolate sauce.

1257
00:44:36,043 --> 00:44:37,779
- [Mike] Honey, you up?

1258
00:44:37,779 --> 00:44:40,779
- George Hamilton finally over tans.

1259
00:44:41,793 --> 00:44:43,793
Death of a kabuki actor.

1260
00:44:48,438 --> 00:44:49,779
- [Tom Servo] Coroner need to know?

1261
00:44:49,779 --> 00:44:50,612
Nah.

1262
00:44:53,754 --> 00:44:56,961
- I'd like to say a few
words, um, this guy is dead.

1263
00:44:56,961 --> 00:44:57,794
The end.

1264
00:44:59,292 --> 00:45:00,977
- [Mike] Well, happy Arbor Day.

1265
00:45:00,977 --> 00:45:02,528
- [Tom Servo] What was that
waiter’s name in Paris?

1266
00:45:02,528 --> 00:45:03,361
Jean-Luc!

1267
00:45:06,861 --> 00:45:08,556
- [Mike] Hey Gary, does this strike you as

1268
00:45:08,556 --> 00:45:11,639
a really gross planet we're invading?

1269
00:45:15,148 --> 00:45:18,737
- [Tom Servo] Wait what am I doing, geez.

1270
00:45:18,737 --> 00:45:20,092
- [Mike] You okay?

1271
00:45:20,092 --> 00:45:22,761
- I'm coming down, thanks.

1272
00:45:22,761 --> 00:45:25,199
- [Mike] They keep their
garbage in the refrigerator?

1273
00:45:25,199 --> 00:45:28,725
- [Tom Servo] An afternoon
with Sondra Locke.

1274
00:45:28,725 --> 00:45:30,166
- I'm not looking, repeat,

1275
00:45:30,166 --> 00:45:32,734
not looking at the
contents of the blender.

1276
00:45:32,734 --> 00:45:34,228
- [Mike] These people
are really the backbone

1277
00:45:34,228 --> 00:45:35,922
of your casino based economy.

1278
00:45:35,922 --> 00:45:36,755
- What's the matter with you?

1279
00:45:36,755 --> 00:45:37,953
- I just caught a glimpse of myself

1280
00:45:37,953 --> 00:45:39,786
in the hallway mirror.

1281
00:45:42,727 --> 00:45:44,146
- [Mike] If I know that spider,

1282
00:45:44,146 --> 00:45:46,192
it’s not a virgin Bloody Mary.

1283
00:45:46,192 --> 00:45:47,690
- Woo hoo.

1284
00:45:47,690 --> 00:45:49,478
- [Tom Servo] Wee!

1285
00:45:49,478 --> 00:45:53,281
- We still on for the
Richard Feynman lecture?

1286
00:45:53,281 --> 00:45:54,928
- You look like you could use a drink.

1287
00:45:54,928 --> 00:45:57,911
- [Tom Servo] And a shower, and a job.

1288
00:45:57,911 --> 00:45:59,761
- I found another body.

1289
00:45:59,761 --> 00:46:01,472
- [Mike] Good, yours is
getting pretty gross.

1290
00:46:01,472 --> 00:46:02,639
- Another cow?

1291
00:46:03,714 --> 00:46:05,017
- A human body.

1292
00:46:05,017 --> 00:46:07,757
- It was walking along the
street and I killed it.

1293
00:46:07,757 --> 00:46:08,603
- A person?

1294
00:46:08,603 --> 00:46:09,634
- [Tom Servo] And Dutch would only give me

1295
00:46:09,634 --> 00:46:11,690
39 cents a pound.

1296
00:46:11,690 --> 00:46:15,722
- But it was chewed up
worse than them cattle.

1297
00:46:15,722 --> 00:46:18,646
- [Mike] Funny, I used
to like things like that.

1298
00:46:18,646 --> 00:46:20,012
- We have to call the sheriff.

1299
00:46:20,012 --> 00:46:22,523
- Are you out of your mind?

1300
00:46:22,523 --> 00:46:26,032
I buried that body and
I hid the motorcycle.

1301
00:46:26,032 --> 00:46:27,797
No one will ever know.

1302
00:46:27,797 --> 00:46:29,185
- You're crazy.

1303
00:46:29,185 --> 00:46:32,768
- We can't let that sheriff
come nosing around here.

1304
00:46:32,768 --> 00:46:35,218
He could find the diamonds

1305
00:46:35,218 --> 00:46:36,685
and all that grass we're growing.

1306
00:46:36,685 --> 00:46:38,231
- [Tom Servo] Wands are
illegal in Wisconsin?

1307
00:46:38,231 --> 00:46:41,529
- You sound like you've been
smoking the stuff yourself.

1308
00:46:41,529 --> 00:46:44,196
- Whoa, my Bloody Mary has legs!

1309
00:46:48,193 --> 00:46:51,146
♫ Waa-waa-waa, waa-waa-waa-waa ♫

1310
00:46:51,146 --> 00:46:53,326
- [Mike] Charlotte is
doing bachelor parties now.

1311
00:46:53,326 --> 00:46:55,086
- [Tom Servo] Pa pom, pa pom, pa pom.

1312
00:46:55,086 --> 00:46:59,003
- The family in Tobacco Road
had a nicer farm than this.

1313
00:46:59,003 --> 00:47:02,401
- [Mike] Hey, pal, you
got any curds and whey?

1314
00:47:02,401 --> 00:47:06,740
- [Tom Servo] He’s doing
kind of a grunge Amish look.

1315
00:47:06,740 --> 00:47:09,062
- My assignment: Take out the greasy hick

1316
00:47:09,062 --> 00:47:10,700
with extreme prejudice.

1317
00:47:10,700 --> 00:47:13,950
- [Mike] I'm proud to be a crap farmer.

1318
00:47:14,985 --> 00:47:17,722
- [Tom Servo] Please sir,
you're standing on my wife.

1319
00:47:17,722 --> 00:47:18,972
- Shine mister?

1320
00:47:21,683 --> 00:47:23,549
(raven caws)

1321
00:47:23,549 --> 00:47:25,192
- [Mike] Why is he cawing?

1322
00:47:25,192 --> 00:47:26,300
- [Tom Servo] I attempted the north face

1323
00:47:26,300 --> 00:47:27,967
of Mount Cheesehead.

1324
00:47:29,004 --> 00:47:31,837
- [Mike] Gee, Mr. Touchy wigs out.

1325
00:47:32,808 --> 00:47:35,066
- Hoo, Ha, missed me!

1326
00:47:35,066 --> 00:47:35,899
Hoo! (laughs)

1327
00:47:35,899 --> 00:47:38,468
- Every creeping thing that
creepeth upon the Earth

1328
00:47:38,468 --> 00:47:40,292
shall be an abomination!

1329
00:47:40,292 --> 00:47:41,664
- [Tom Servo] Gotta nip it in the bud!

1330
00:47:41,664 --> 00:47:46,252
- [Preacher] Only the pure
of heart shall be spared.

1331
00:47:46,252 --> 00:47:49,502
- Spider's barbecue got out of control.

1332
00:47:50,378 --> 00:47:51,783
- Oh it's you.

1333
00:47:51,783 --> 00:47:53,079
- [Mike] Don Juan de Stinko.

1334
00:47:53,079 --> 00:47:55,046
- I told ya I could come again tonight.

1335
00:47:55,046 --> 00:47:55,879
- No. (groans)

1336
00:47:55,879 --> 00:47:57,267
- How'd you swing it honey?

1337
00:47:57,267 --> 00:47:59,832
- Well I told the lush
that I had to come in

1338
00:47:59,832 --> 00:48:02,429
and see my cousin about some hot rocks.

1339
00:48:02,429 --> 00:48:06,014
- [Mike, Tom Servo, Crow] (groaning)

1340
00:48:06,014 --> 00:48:08,653
- Come on in, let's do your taxes.

1341
00:48:08,653 --> 00:48:12,820
(Tom Servo hums "Dueling
Banjos" by Arthur Smith)

1342
00:48:15,870 --> 00:48:17,189
- [Mike] That's a cute room.

1343
00:48:17,189 --> 00:48:19,285
And the whiskey bottle,
just the right touch.

1344
00:48:19,285 --> 00:48:22,577
- Is this Annette Benning’s
bedroom from In Style magazine?

1345
00:48:22,577 --> 00:48:23,518
- [Tom Servo] She ran out of liquor,

1346
00:48:23,518 --> 00:48:26,185
so she’s drinking her Jean Nate.

1347
00:48:29,425 --> 00:48:31,758
- [Mike] No, that's the bed!

1348
00:48:33,904 --> 00:48:37,163
- The Martha Stewart we never see.

1349
00:48:37,163 --> 00:48:40,346
- [Tom Servo] I'll hang
those up over there.

1350
00:48:40,346 --> 00:48:42,614
- [Mike] The spiders
using all eight eyes now,

1351
00:48:42,614 --> 00:48:44,829
I can tell you that.

1352
00:48:44,829 --> 00:48:48,996
♫ I enjoy being a victim ♫

1353
00:48:50,954 --> 00:48:52,192
Invade!

1354
00:48:52,192 --> 00:48:53,275
G-guys, guys?

1355
00:48:54,439 --> 00:48:56,177
♫ I feel shaky

1356
00:48:56,177 --> 00:48:57,759
♫ Oh so trembly

1357
00:48:57,759 --> 00:49:01,354
♫ I’ve had whiskey and vodka and gin ♫

1358
00:49:01,354 --> 00:49:02,886
- [Mike] The house is
decorated with the special

1359
00:49:02,886 --> 00:49:04,806
Jim Varney Signature Collection.

1360
00:49:04,806 --> 00:49:06,239
- [Tom Servo] You and I are very alike.

1361
00:49:06,239 --> 00:49:07,072
Join me!

1362
00:49:12,284 --> 00:49:14,374
- [Mike] This invasion
is awfully sluggish.

1363
00:49:14,374 --> 00:49:17,457
It's more like a minor spider unrest.

1364
00:49:18,629 --> 00:49:20,845
- Maybe if I left him little love notes,

1365
00:49:20,845 --> 00:49:23,178
throw pork rinds on the bed.

1366
00:49:25,600 --> 00:49:27,044
- [Mike] I'm seeing two beds!

1367
00:49:27,044 --> 00:49:28,154
Oh, there are.

1368
00:49:28,154 --> 00:49:29,583
- Is there a Japanese tea ceremony

1369
00:49:29,583 --> 00:49:31,500
taking place next door?

1370
00:49:32,351 --> 00:49:34,007
- [Tom Servo] Tonight
the battle came through

1371
00:49:34,007 --> 00:49:36,011
in a big way, hoo!

1372
00:49:36,011 --> 00:49:37,226
- [Mike] What was I doing?

1373
00:49:37,226 --> 00:49:41,024
I wasn't drinking there for a second.

1374
00:49:41,024 --> 00:49:42,727
- [Tom Servo] Are we panning
down to her ab Roller?

1375
00:49:42,727 --> 00:49:44,894
What the hell is going on?

1376
00:49:46,281 --> 00:49:47,641
- Bill Rebane's trademark,

1377
00:49:47,641 --> 00:49:50,141
a shot of crumpled underpants.

1378
00:49:51,981 --> 00:49:52,814
- [Mike] What's that?

1379
00:49:52,814 --> 00:49:55,587
If you insist, I'll have a drink, thanks.

1380
00:49:55,587 --> 00:49:57,052
Does the Fonz usually sleep here

1381
00:49:57,052 --> 00:49:59,635
with his head against the wall?

1382
00:50:00,904 --> 00:50:01,814
- Well, I'm feeling better.

1383
00:50:01,814 --> 00:50:04,560
At least I'm not seeing spiders tonight.

1384
00:50:04,560 --> 00:50:08,727
- [Tom Servo] Well, gotta get
up early to start drinking.

1385
00:50:12,074 --> 00:50:14,134
- I need a new pillow.

1386
00:50:14,134 --> 00:50:15,461
And bed.

1387
00:50:15,461 --> 00:50:16,294
House.

1388
00:50:17,237 --> 00:50:18,213
Husband.

1389
00:50:18,213 --> 00:50:19,046
Life.

1390
00:50:19,921 --> 00:50:22,467
- [Tom Servo] Tora tora tora!

1391
00:50:22,467 --> 00:50:23,787
- [Mike] Spider, cut it out honey.

1392
00:50:23,787 --> 00:50:24,822
I'm tired.

1393
00:50:24,822 --> 00:50:28,072
- Every night his legs are all over me.

1394
00:50:31,730 --> 00:50:34,563
- [Tom Servo] Securing butt, over.

1395
00:50:38,683 --> 00:50:41,400
I wish they hadn't led us
down the giant spider path

1396
00:50:41,400 --> 00:50:42,942
if they couldn't deliver one.

1397
00:50:42,942 --> 00:50:44,691
- [Mike] I think they were
saying that a giant spider

1398
00:50:44,691 --> 00:50:46,282
would be nice but as an alternative

1399
00:50:46,282 --> 00:50:49,028
please consider our little movie.

1400
00:50:49,028 --> 00:50:50,945
- Music budget ran out.

1401
00:50:52,527 --> 00:50:53,360
- (screams

1402
00:50:53,360 --> 00:50:54,830
- [Tom Servo] We're your
dirty socks, wash us!

1403
00:50:54,830 --> 00:50:56,830
- Giant puppet invasion.

1404
00:50:59,591 --> 00:51:00,882
(screaming)

1405
00:51:00,882 --> 00:51:03,257
- [Mike] Yeah, I know lady,
it's not my web, honest.

1406
00:51:03,257 --> 00:51:05,674
I'm caught in this thing too.

1407
00:51:06,742 --> 00:51:08,548
- Tonight, on a very special Waltons,

1408
00:51:08,548 --> 00:51:12,426
Mary Ellen runs around in her underwear.

1409
00:51:12,426 --> 00:51:14,037
- [Mike] Mr. Lincoln, Mr. Lincoln!

1410
00:51:14,037 --> 00:51:15,507
Abe!

1411
00:51:15,507 --> 00:51:18,126
- Okay let's see, it's
darker in here, danker.

1412
00:51:18,126 --> 00:51:22,407
No there won't be any
spiders in here, no siree.

1413
00:51:22,407 --> 00:51:23,266
(screaming)

1414
00:51:23,266 --> 00:51:24,991
- My novelty throw pillow!

1415
00:51:24,991 --> 00:51:29,554
- [Mike] I’m a Woozle,
and my name is Peanut.

1416
00:51:29,554 --> 00:51:31,329
- It’s morning in America.

1417
00:51:31,329 --> 00:51:33,070
The back braces are a little sturdier.

1418
00:51:33,070 --> 00:51:35,290
- [Tom Servo] The morning
gin tastes a little smoother.

1419
00:51:35,290 --> 00:51:37,957
- Hey you forgot something.

1420
00:51:37,957 --> 00:51:39,985
- No, I got it on.

1421
00:51:39,985 --> 00:51:41,528
- Your hard drugs.

1422
00:51:41,528 --> 00:51:43,041
- Oh, thank you.

1423
00:51:43,041 --> 00:51:44,935
I always give you a big tip.

1424
00:51:44,935 --> 00:51:46,481
- [Mike] Here's your navel lint.

1425
00:51:46,481 --> 00:51:47,792
- Thank you darling.

1426
00:51:47,792 --> 00:51:50,081
- [Tom Servo] So this
is how Heidi turned out.

1427
00:51:50,081 --> 00:51:53,498
(instrumental pop music)

1428
00:51:58,336 --> 00:52:01,532
- [Tom Servo] Back braces
steamed and cleaned, here it is.

1429
00:52:01,532 --> 00:52:04,115
- [Mike] My old boss Mr. Gower.

1430
00:52:05,301 --> 00:52:06,473
- Cousin Dan.

1431
00:52:06,473 --> 00:52:07,422
- Cousin Eddie.

1432
00:52:07,422 --> 00:52:09,724
- What brings you to town?

1433
00:52:09,724 --> 00:52:11,982
Hey, how's that hot little tomato

1434
00:52:11,982 --> 00:52:13,542
you're raising out there, huh?

1435
00:52:13,542 --> 00:52:14,776
- [Tom Servo] Does he raise tomatoes?

1436
00:52:14,776 --> 00:52:16,541
- Terry is way overripe for picking.

1437
00:52:16,541 --> 00:52:18,014
- [Tom Servo] I didn't
know he raised tomatoes.

1438
00:52:18,014 --> 00:52:20,844
- Terry's turning bad, I
can't control her anymore.

1439
00:52:20,844 --> 00:52:23,802
- Well, she needs a
gentle hand, like mine.

1440
00:52:23,802 --> 00:52:26,341
- [Tom Servo, Mike, Crow] (retching)

1441
00:52:26,341 --> 00:52:28,747
- Here I got something I want to show you.

1442
00:52:28,747 --> 00:52:29,705
What is that?

1443
00:52:29,705 --> 00:52:30,538
- That?

1444
00:52:30,538 --> 00:52:31,620
That's a geode.

1445
00:52:31,620 --> 00:52:32,690
That's not from around here.

1446
00:52:32,690 --> 00:52:34,065
- So let's beat it up!

1447
00:52:34,065 --> 00:52:37,049
- You must have found that
down south someplace huh?

1448
00:52:37,049 --> 00:52:38,606
- Take a look at these.

1449
00:52:38,606 --> 00:52:41,391
Just how good are these diamonds here?

1450
00:52:41,391 --> 00:52:42,680
- [Tom Servo] Are they worth two months

1451
00:52:42,680 --> 00:52:44,459
of my welfare checks?

1452
00:52:44,459 --> 00:52:46,313
- [Mike] The diamond anniversary ring.

1453
00:52:46,313 --> 00:52:48,367
Tell her you’d marry her
right out of high school

1454
00:52:48,367 --> 00:52:49,617
all over again.

1455
00:52:52,397 --> 00:52:53,673
- [Tom Servo] Oh, just
seeing an old fingernail

1456
00:52:53,673 --> 00:52:54,561
with dirt under it.

1457
00:52:54,561 --> 00:52:56,311
Oh, wait that's mine.

1458
00:52:57,465 --> 00:53:00,965
- So, seen Leatherface around here lately?

1459
00:53:03,222 --> 00:53:06,073
- Now, just between you and me,

1460
00:53:06,073 --> 00:53:06,906
- Yeah?

1461
00:53:07,781 --> 00:53:10,022
- (blows raspberry)

1462
00:53:10,022 --> 00:53:12,323
- [Tom Servo] Sir, you offend me!

1463
00:53:12,323 --> 00:53:14,740
- They're industrial quality.

1464
00:53:16,176 --> 00:53:18,524
I mean the carbon content
isn't nearly as high

1465
00:53:18,524 --> 00:53:22,470
as a real diamond, a ring type diamond.

1466
00:53:22,470 --> 00:53:23,872
- [Mike] Charles Manson, jeweler.

1467
00:53:23,872 --> 00:53:25,404
- How much are they worth?

1468
00:53:25,404 --> 00:53:29,793
- Well, let's just say, if you
had a bucket full of these,

1469
00:53:29,793 --> 00:53:31,025
a barrel full of these,

1470
00:53:31,025 --> 00:53:31,990
- [Tom Servo] You’d be a fat cheesehead

1471
00:53:31,990 --> 00:53:33,215
with a barrel full of these.

1472
00:53:33,215 --> 00:53:34,836
- Yeah, you might be rich.

1473
00:53:34,836 --> 00:53:36,300
Where'd you find these?

1474
00:53:36,300 --> 00:53:39,800
- Let's just say they fell out of the sky.

1475
00:53:41,556 --> 00:53:43,431
- Ha ha, well met my friend!

1476
00:53:43,431 --> 00:53:45,764
This battle of wits is over.

1477
00:53:47,200 --> 00:53:48,728
(electronic humming)

1478
00:53:48,728 --> 00:53:52,286
♫ Ooh, what a lucky man he was ♫

1479
00:53:52,286 --> 00:53:53,944
- What's going on now?

1480
00:53:53,944 --> 00:53:55,237
- [Dr. Langer] Those satellite reports

1481
00:53:55,237 --> 00:53:56,663
you asked Paul Rider to send.

1482
00:53:56,663 --> 00:53:57,496
- [Mike] Oh, goodie.

1483
00:53:57,496 --> 00:54:00,774
Back to the really unappealing characters.

1484
00:54:00,774 --> 00:54:01,722
- Let me see that.

1485
00:54:01,722 --> 00:54:03,561
- [Tom Servo] Dear Chunkhead,
well that's not nice!

1486
00:54:03,561 --> 00:54:06,827
- Latitude 45 degrees 21 minutes west.

1487
00:54:06,827 --> 00:54:08,549
Correction north.

1488
00:54:08,549 --> 00:54:11,536
Longitude 88 degrees 42 minutes west,

1489
00:54:11,536 --> 00:54:13,438
that's more than a couple of square miles.

1490
00:54:13,438 --> 00:54:14,521
- I know.

1491
00:54:14,521 --> 00:54:16,241
- Can we pinpoint it closer than that?

1492
00:54:16,241 --> 00:54:17,971
- Not from Telcom.

1493
00:54:17,971 --> 00:54:19,994
I'm afraid you're going to
have to use a helicopter.

1494
00:54:19,994 --> 00:54:21,686
- [Mike] (laughs) Let's have some tea.

1495
00:54:21,686 --> 00:54:22,519
- [Crow] Tea.

1496
00:54:22,519 --> 00:54:23,352
- Okay.

1497
00:54:23,352 --> 00:54:24,185
- [Tom Servo] There must be an easier way

1498
00:54:24,185 --> 00:54:25,235
to find the Angler's Bar.

1499
00:54:25,235 --> 00:54:26,310
- Paul Rider please.

1500
00:54:26,310 --> 00:54:27,203
- Paul Reiser!

1501
00:54:27,203 --> 00:54:28,665
This is a horror movie!

1502
00:54:28,665 --> 00:54:30,631
(dog barking)

1503
00:54:30,631 --> 00:54:32,016
- [Mike] Ed Wood’s Lolita.

1504
00:54:32,016 --> 00:54:34,038
- Where the hell is Ev?

1505
00:54:34,038 --> 00:54:35,288
- I don't know.

1506
00:54:36,620 --> 00:54:37,544
- [Mike] Oh, she's putting out

1507
