2002
01:13:00,172 --> 01:13:02,332
R. Crumb is leading them!

2003
01:13:02,332 --> 01:13:04,754
- [Mike] For grandma Schmeekar!

2004
01:13:04,754 --> 01:13:06,505
- [Tom Servo] Let's just kill each other!

2005
01:13:06,505 --> 01:13:07,668
(shouting and yelling)

2006
01:13:07,668 --> 01:13:08,958
- [Voiceover] Like I said inside,

2007
01:13:08,958 --> 01:13:11,024
I want each of you to go
in different directions.

2008
01:13:11,024 --> 01:13:13,786
I want you to get your friends,
relatives, anyone you can!

2009
01:13:13,786 --> 01:13:17,286
- What if my friends don't have relatives?

2010
01:13:17,286 --> 01:13:19,908
- [Voiceover] Dutch, what's going on?

2011
01:13:19,908 --> 01:13:22,973
- [Mike, Tom Servo, Crow]
Packers! Whoo! Go Packers!

2012
01:13:22,973 --> 01:13:24,361
- Dutch you're a troublemaker.

2013
01:13:24,361 --> 01:13:25,751
I'm trying to tell you to knock it off!

2014
01:13:25,751 --> 01:13:27,215
Now everybody go home...

2015
01:13:27,215 --> 01:13:29,925
(shouting and yelling)

2016
01:13:29,925 --> 01:13:32,466
- [Sheriff] Knock it off!
- [Dutch] You knock it off!

2017
01:13:32,466 --> 01:13:33,880
- All right, let's go, come on!

2018
01:13:33,880 --> 01:13:35,261
- [Mike] Wait a minute, we can't hunt,

2019
01:13:35,261 --> 01:13:37,056
we're not drunk enough yet.

2020
01:13:37,056 --> 01:13:41,139
- [Tom Servo, Mike, Crow]
Packers! Whoo! Packers!

2021
01:13:42,449 --> 01:13:43,896
- [Mike] Please, if you
would all just go back

2022
01:13:43,896 --> 01:13:45,876
to your drinking!

2023
01:13:45,876 --> 01:13:47,205
(yelling, tires screeching)

2024
01:13:47,205 --> 01:13:48,719
- [Sheriff] Alright everybody just--

2025
01:13:48,719 --> 01:13:50,469
- Wang chung tonight!

2026
01:13:53,580 --> 01:13:58,485
- [Tom Servo] It's Old
Milwaukee coming out of there.

2027
01:13:58,485 --> 01:14:00,949
Just swing us till we die.

2028
01:14:00,949 --> 01:14:02,611
(carnival music)

2029
01:14:02,611 --> 01:14:04,341
- Ride the vomit rainbow!

2030
01:14:04,341 --> 01:14:08,834
Strolling bands of technicolor
yawns splayed across the sky.

2031
01:14:08,834 --> 01:14:10,471
- [Tom Servo] Hopefully
we'll work up enough speed

2032
01:14:10,471 --> 01:14:13,683
to launch us into Minnesota
and start a real life!

2033
01:14:13,683 --> 01:14:16,638
- [Mike] It's been an
hour, please let us down.

2034
01:14:16,638 --> 01:14:18,921
- You know carnies are the
most respected citizens

2035
01:14:18,921 --> 01:14:20,004
of this town.

2036
01:14:22,578 --> 01:14:24,761
- [Tom Servo] Honk, honk, vroom!

2037
01:14:24,761 --> 01:14:27,730
- [Mike] It’s Suicide
Days in New Richmond.

2038
01:14:27,730 --> 01:14:30,736
- I wanna go pet the wounded goat.

2039
01:14:30,736 --> 01:14:34,903
- [Mike] Are you sure that's
as fast as this thing can go?

2040
01:14:37,785 --> 01:14:40,015
- [Tom Servo] Beck!

2041
01:14:40,015 --> 01:14:42,265
- It’s Milling Around Days.

2042
01:14:43,957 --> 01:14:46,591
- [Tom Servo] The Lions Club
medium-rare chicken booth.

2043
01:14:46,591 --> 01:14:48,263
- Free range and beer fed.

2044
01:14:48,263 --> 01:14:51,846
- [Mike] Basted with
sun brewed mayonnaise.

2045
01:14:54,484 --> 01:14:56,544
- [Tom Servo] Despair
Days is fun this year!

2046
01:14:56,544 --> 01:14:59,445
- [Crow] Nom, nom, nom, nom.

2047
01:14:59,445 --> 01:15:03,612
This is where you'd find
a crocheted beer can hat.

2048
01:15:06,043 --> 01:15:08,543
- [Tom Servo] How sweet it is!

2049
01:15:11,352 --> 01:15:13,693
- [Mike] And the score is 78-5

2050
01:15:13,693 --> 01:15:16,015
in the bottom of the 3rd inning.

2051
01:15:16,015 --> 01:15:17,848
- Packers won the Superbowl!

2052
01:15:17,848 --> 01:15:19,903
- [Tom] Packers! Yaay!

2053
01:15:19,903 --> 01:15:23,403
Previously owned cheese curds are on sale!

2054
01:15:24,708 --> 01:15:25,678
- Woo, he stood up.

2055
01:15:25,678 --> 01:15:28,286
He's got to get hazard pay for this.

2056
01:15:28,286 --> 01:15:30,028
- [Mike] I think I had
a hot dog in here once.

2057
01:15:30,028 --> 01:15:31,689
(telephone Ringing)

2058
01:15:31,689 --> 01:15:32,734
- [Tom Servo] He could do a one-man show

2059
01:15:32,734 --> 01:15:35,028
playing Queen Victoria.

2060
01:15:35,028 --> 01:15:37,193
- Hello, yeah this is the Sheriff.

2061
01:15:37,193 --> 01:15:39,606
- You've discovered a new kind of meat?

2062
01:15:39,606 --> 01:15:40,439
- What?

2063
01:15:40,439 --> 01:15:41,743
- [Mike] Pork gravy from a can?

2064
01:15:41,743 --> 01:15:42,755
- In Gleason?

2065
01:15:42,755 --> 01:15:44,383
- [Tom Servo] Does Jackie mind?

2066
01:15:44,383 --> 01:15:46,327
- Are you sure they're headed this way?

2067
01:15:46,327 --> 01:15:48,382
- Did they bring a dish to pass?

2068
01:15:48,382 --> 01:15:49,215
- Okay.

2069
01:15:50,090 --> 01:15:51,360
(frenzied screams and shouts)

2070
01:15:51,360 --> 01:15:53,327
- [Mike] It's a cheese-fueled mob frenzy!

2071
01:15:53,327 --> 01:15:57,244
- [Tom Servo] Welcome to
Beer Hall Putsch Days!

2072
01:16:00,745 --> 01:16:02,162
- John Malkovich!

2073
01:16:03,032 --> 01:16:04,967
- Hello operator?
- [Mike] Where's Gleason?

2074
01:16:04,967 --> 01:16:08,787
- Give me the National Guard
headquarters in Madison.

2075
01:16:08,787 --> 01:16:11,658
- [Tom Servo] When
snowmobilers drive cars.

2076
01:16:11,658 --> 01:16:15,205
- Now you really can't
blame a spider for that.

2077
01:16:15,205 --> 01:16:16,095
- [Mike] Too late.

2078
01:16:16,095 --> 01:16:19,428
Insurgents overthrew the Baraboo regime.

2079
01:16:21,493 --> 01:16:22,743
- Patrick, hey.

2080
01:16:24,244 --> 01:16:26,669
- [Tom Servo] He's them organs,
we didn't put them on ice.

2081
01:16:26,669 --> 01:16:28,252
I hope that's okay.

2082
01:16:29,104 --> 01:16:32,806
Here take some zucchini,
we have so much this year.

2083
01:16:32,806 --> 01:16:36,889
- By the way, this is
Wisconsin’s National Guard.

2084
01:16:38,081 --> 01:16:39,608
- [Tom Servo] Audiences won't soon forget

2085
01:16:39,608 --> 01:16:41,447
when the thing we didn't know what it was,

2086
01:16:41,447 --> 01:16:45,614
was put in the helicopter
by the guy we didn't know.

2087
01:16:49,655 --> 01:16:52,307
- [Crow] Are we dead Mike?

2088
01:16:52,307 --> 01:16:53,404
- [Voiceover] Once you seal of the hole,

2089
01:16:53,404 --> 01:16:54,427
what's going to happen with the spiders?

2090
01:16:54,427 --> 01:16:57,706
(cackling and rasping)

2091
01:16:57,706 --> 01:17:00,498
- [Dr. Vance] Once we seal
that hole, they're gone.

2092
01:17:00,498 --> 01:17:02,279
- [Dr. Langer] But what if
the initiator doesn't work?

2093
01:17:02,279 --> 01:17:03,833
There's going to be an
army of those spiders

2094
01:17:03,833 --> 01:17:05,775
crawling around growing and multiplying.

2095
01:17:05,775 --> 01:17:08,025
- [Mike] Rebane was filming
night for night here, wasn’t he?

2096
01:17:08,025 --> 01:17:10,057
- [Dr. Vance] Look honey,
it's already happening.

2097
01:17:10,057 --> 01:17:12,640
- [Crow] It's Dr. Honey to you.

2098
01:17:14,779 --> 01:17:15,612
- [Tom Servo] Oh, no!

2099
01:17:15,612 --> 01:17:17,197
It's a fish boil.

2100
01:17:17,197 --> 01:17:20,980
- [Mike] We don't have to put
our nuclear waste into casks.

2101
01:17:20,980 --> 01:17:23,732
- [Crow] Dark, it's not
dark Rebane declared.

2102
01:17:23,732 --> 01:17:25,199
- [Tom Servo] Visuals for a movie?

2103
01:17:25,199 --> 01:17:26,449
Who needs them?

2104
01:17:27,874 --> 01:17:32,512
- [Mike] And somewhere in the
world a helicopter exists.

2105
01:17:32,512 --> 01:17:35,245
- Lord knows how many of
those things are around here.

2106
01:17:35,245 --> 01:17:36,449
- Just take it easy.

2107
01:17:36,449 --> 01:17:37,804
- [Tom Servo] Let’s you
and I go up to Rhinelander

2108
01:17:37,804 --> 01:17:39,712
and roll on each other.

2109
01:17:39,712 --> 01:17:41,297
- Oh look at this stuff.

2110
01:17:41,297 --> 01:17:43,462
- [Crow] When grandmas go spelunking.

2111
01:17:43,462 --> 01:17:44,295
- [Dr. Langer] Oh!

2112
01:17:44,295 --> 01:17:45,175
- [Dr. Vance] What's the matter?

2113
01:17:45,175 --> 01:17:46,779
- [Mike] Quit falling on me!

2114
01:17:46,779 --> 01:17:49,320
- [Dr. Langer] (screaming)
- [Dr. Vance] My god!

2115
01:17:49,320 --> 01:17:50,956
God another one.

2116
01:17:50,956 --> 01:17:52,276
- Let's get out of here.

2117
01:17:52,276 --> 01:17:54,850
- [Tom Servo] Let’s go have
a nice dinner at the Gobbler.

2118
01:17:54,850 --> 01:17:57,415
- [Crow] Oh, it's a, huh?

2119
01:17:57,415 --> 01:18:02,265
- [Mike] Robert McNamara
escalates the war on Gleason.

2120
01:18:02,265 --> 01:18:06,432
- [Tom Servo] Can we roll the
rest of the way to the car?

2121
01:18:08,440 --> 01:18:11,321
Emergency, I am winded
and I am very moist.

2122
01:18:11,321 --> 01:18:13,455
- Patch me through to the Sheriff.

2123
01:18:13,455 --> 01:18:15,577
- [Mike] Maybe if I kill
myself, like Hemingway,

2124
01:18:15,577 --> 01:18:18,276
people will remember me fondly.

2125
01:18:18,276 --> 01:18:19,234
(telephone ringing)

2126
01:18:19,234 --> 01:18:21,196
- [Tom Servo] That would be
my shift down at Skipper’s.

2127
01:18:21,196 --> 01:18:25,671
- [Crow] Rebane and Hale,
like Scorsese and De Niro.

2128
01:18:25,671 --> 01:18:26,504
- Hello.

2129
01:18:26,504 --> 01:18:28,206
(Tom Servo makes farting noises)

2130
01:18:28,206 --> 01:18:29,039
- Yeah, Vance.

2131
01:18:29,039 --> 01:18:30,360
- [Mike] I'm sitting.

2132
01:18:30,360 --> 01:18:32,635
- The spiders are all over in Gleason.

2133
01:18:32,635 --> 01:18:33,928
Just a few miles away.

2134
01:18:33,928 --> 01:18:35,678
- [Crow] I’ll drive my Lark there.

2135
01:18:35,678 --> 01:18:38,676
- Yes, I've called for the National Guard.

2136
01:18:38,676 --> 01:18:39,634
- [Mike] But he's not in.

2137
01:18:39,634 --> 01:18:40,467
- The mobs are beginning to gather

2138
01:18:40,467 --> 01:18:41,769
and they are getting out of hand.

2139
01:18:41,769 --> 01:18:43,060
- Look, get somebody out here.

2140
01:18:43,060 --> 01:18:45,857
I just found another body
or what's left of one.

2141
01:18:45,857 --> 01:18:49,497
And for God's sake, keep
that mob away from here.

2142
01:18:49,497 --> 01:18:52,312
- [Crow] It's more of a mob (mumbles)

2143
01:18:52,312 --> 01:18:56,020
- [Mike] The mob demands Whoopee John.

2144
01:18:56,020 --> 01:18:58,291
- [Tom Servo] So they're really
giving over to mob mentality

2145
01:18:58,291 --> 01:19:00,541
to stand around and mingle.

2146
01:19:02,294 --> 01:19:06,732
- [Tom Servo, Mike, Crow]
Packers! Whoo! Packers!

2147
01:19:06,732 --> 01:19:09,482
(crowd shouting)

2148
01:19:11,483 --> 01:19:13,271
- [Dutch] You know why we’re all here.

2149
01:19:13,271 --> 01:19:18,229
- [Tom Servo, Mike, Crow]
Yeah, Packers! Packers! Whoo!

2150
01:19:18,229 --> 01:19:22,084
- [Dutch] You've all got your
guns, they're all loaded.

2151
01:19:22,084 --> 01:19:25,863
- [Mike] The margarine riot of 1974.

2152
01:19:25,863 --> 01:19:27,183
- [Crow] Free Bobby Seale!

2153
01:19:27,183 --> 01:19:28,141
- [Tom Servo] Free Mumia!

2154
01:19:28,141 --> 01:19:29,724
- [Crow] Free beer!

2155
01:19:29,724 --> 01:19:30,557
- [Sheriff] Come on now Dutch,

2156
01:19:30,557 --> 01:19:31,916
I want you to get out of here, all of you!

2157
01:19:31,916 --> 01:19:34,178
- [Tom Servo] They’re toughening
GED standards, no fair!

2158
01:19:34,178 --> 01:19:35,011
Boo!

2159
01:19:35,011 --> 01:19:37,941
- [Tom Servo, Mike, Crow]
Packers! Whoo! Packers!

2160
01:19:37,941 --> 01:19:40,588
- [Sheriff] I got a man from
NASA who knows what he's doing.

2161
01:19:40,588 --> 01:19:42,353
Gleason is a disaster area,

2162
01:19:42,353 --> 01:19:44,037
- [Tom Servo] Packers! Whoo!

2163
01:19:44,037 --> 01:19:45,308
- [Dutch] We'll handle it ourselves.

2164
01:19:45,308 --> 01:19:46,141
Come on!

2165
01:19:46,141 --> 01:19:49,222
- [Tom Servo] US out of
North America and Packers!

2166
01:19:49,222 --> 01:19:50,414
No more schools!

2167
01:19:50,414 --> 01:19:52,219
More hockey arenas!

2168
01:19:52,219 --> 01:19:53,302
More Packers!

2169
01:19:54,590 --> 01:19:56,292
- Well it got hit by the monster.

2170
01:19:56,292 --> 01:19:57,631
The crowd is getting out of hand.

2171
01:19:57,631 --> 01:19:59,199
I can't control 'em.

2172
01:19:59,199 --> 01:20:01,749
They're hellbent on destroying that beast.

2173
01:20:01,749 --> 01:20:02,863
- [Tom Servo] They're hellbent.

2174
01:20:02,863 --> 01:20:04,409
- You ever see the movie Jaws?

2175
01:20:04,409 --> 01:20:07,639
Well it makes that shark
look like a goldfish!

2176
01:20:07,639 --> 01:20:09,551
- I know, I know.

2177
01:20:09,551 --> 01:20:10,384
- The better movie.

2178
01:20:10,384 --> 01:20:11,644
Try to keep them there as long as you can.

2179
01:20:11,644 --> 01:20:13,238
We're setting up the lights around here

2180
01:20:13,238 --> 01:20:14,695
and the bomb is on it's way.

2181
01:20:14,695 --> 01:20:16,657
And try to keep the spider there.

2182
01:20:16,657 --> 01:20:18,421
- [Sheriff] We can't do
anything with the spider.

2183
01:20:18,421 --> 01:20:19,498
Bullets don't hurt it.

2184
01:20:19,498 --> 01:20:21,199
The only thing I've got
to stop them here with

2185
01:20:21,199 --> 01:20:22,391
is a traffic light.

2186
01:20:22,391 --> 01:20:24,548
- Sheriff, at least try.

2187
01:20:24,548 --> 01:20:28,548
- [Tom Servo] There's
baby Earp on his shoulder.

2188
01:20:29,462 --> 01:20:31,310
- Okay, forget it spider, you win, sorry!

2189
01:20:31,310 --> 01:20:32,393
Sorry, sorry.

2190
01:20:33,518 --> 01:20:35,446
- [Sheriff] I'm down here all by myself.

2191
01:20:35,446 --> 01:20:37,029
Call the National Guard back,

2192
01:20:37,029 --> 01:20:38,357
tell them we need some heavy equipment.

2193
01:20:38,357 --> 01:20:40,274
- [Mike] Fur is murder!

2194
01:20:41,776 --> 01:20:43,392
- [Tom Servo] Violence
erupted when Dave Dudley

2195
01:20:43,392 --> 01:20:46,309
canceled his appearance in Gleason.

2196
01:20:48,648 --> 01:20:50,289
- [Mike] I’m headed over to Taco John’s

2197
01:20:50,289 --> 01:20:51,806
till this blows over.

2198
01:20:51,806 --> 01:20:55,223
(instrumental pop music)

2199
01:21:01,766 --> 01:21:04,766
- [Tom Servo] Just honk at it honey.

2200
01:21:06,110 --> 01:21:10,193
- [Mike] Give my Hamm’s
waterfall sign to my son.

2201
01:21:12,525 --> 01:21:14,235
- (gasps) Dutch!

2202
01:21:14,235 --> 01:21:15,587
Oh, Dutch.

2203
01:21:15,587 --> 01:21:16,910
– [Tom Servo] Too many Jell-O shots.

2204
01:21:16,910 --> 01:21:18,540
– [Mike] No more tainted meat sandwiches.

2205
01:21:18,540 --> 01:21:21,926
- [Preacher] Great earthquakes
shall be in diverse places--

2206
01:21:21,926 --> 01:21:22,995
- [Tom Servo] Is there
a verse from the Bible

2207
01:21:22,995 --> 01:21:26,200
that tells us when the
end of this movie is near?

2208
01:21:26,200 --> 01:21:29,308
- [Preacher] And great signs
shall there be from Heaven!

2209
01:21:29,308 --> 01:21:31,948
- The spider is retreating,
heading out of town.

2210
01:21:31,948 --> 01:21:33,527
We've got a lot of people hurt here.

2211
01:21:33,527 --> 01:21:34,735
- [Tom Servo] Somehow
this will all tie back

2212
01:21:34,735 --> 01:21:36,589
to the yellowed back-brace.

2213
01:21:36,589 --> 01:21:37,957
- [Tom Servo] Packers.

2214
01:21:37,957 --> 01:21:39,295
- Packers?

2215
01:21:39,295 --> 01:21:40,128
- Clear the street!

2216
01:21:40,128 --> 01:21:41,897
The spider is gone, the spider is gone!

2217
01:21:41,897 --> 01:21:43,020
Get out of here!

2218
01:21:43,020 --> 01:21:44,017
- [Mike] Um, Mr. Rebane,

2219
01:21:44,017 --> 01:21:45,748
you really can’t see anything.

2220
01:21:45,748 --> 01:21:50,303
– [Tom Servo] Shut up and keep
filming, Mr. NYU Film Pants.

2221
01:21:50,303 --> 01:21:51,261
- [Dr. Langer] You know that big one

2222
01:21:51,261 --> 01:21:53,026
is like a mother queen bee.

2223
01:21:53,026 --> 01:21:54,839
- [Dr. Vance] Yes and she's
activated all the spiders

2224
01:21:54,839 --> 01:21:56,470
in this whole area.

2225
01:21:56,470 --> 01:21:57,303
- [Dr. Langer] Do you
think the smaller ones

2226
01:21:57,303 --> 01:21:58,136
will grow to be giants?

2227
01:21:58,136 --> 01:22:00,954
- Well it could be, unless
that neutron gadget works.

2228
01:22:00,954 --> 01:22:03,474
- I wish that chopper would get here.

2229
01:22:03,474 --> 01:22:05,214
- Here comes somebody now.

2230
01:22:05,214 --> 01:22:07,013
- Why, it's Barney.

2231
01:22:07,013 --> 01:22:09,496
- [Tom Servo] You got to
nip it in the bud, Andy!

2232
01:22:09,496 --> 01:22:11,393
(police siren)

2233
01:22:11,393 --> 01:22:15,681
No, it's my emergency
shipment of Lucky Strikes.

2234
01:22:15,681 --> 01:22:18,929
- Vance, that big one, I just
saw it up on the highway.

2235
01:22:18,929 --> 01:22:20,042
It's cutting through the woods

2236
01:22:20,042 --> 01:22:22,875
and it's headed in this direction.

2237
01:22:24,200 --> 01:22:25,342
- These are just the drunks,

2238
01:22:25,342 --> 01:22:28,731
they haven't even gotten
to the wounded yet.

2239
01:22:28,731 --> 01:22:31,314
- [Mike] It’s a VW in chenille.

2240
01:22:33,348 --> 01:22:34,636
- [Tom Servo] I understand you can repair

2241
01:22:34,636 --> 01:22:37,053
these giant spiders yourself.

2242
01:22:39,353 --> 01:22:40,651
- There comes the chopper now.

2243
01:22:40,651 --> 01:22:42,136
- It's a vegetable chopper though.

2244
01:22:42,136 --> 01:22:42,969
- Can you patch me through?

2245
01:22:42,969 --> 01:22:44,836
- Sure Vance.

2246
01:22:44,836 --> 01:22:45,813
- [Mike] Is this going to be another case

2247
01:22:45,813 --> 01:22:48,599
of a scientist declaring martial law?

2248
01:22:48,599 --> 01:22:51,486
I wish John Agar were in the movie.

2249
01:22:51,486 --> 01:22:52,619
- Cain, this is Vance.

2250
01:22:52,619 --> 01:22:53,857
Cain, this is Vance.

2251
01:22:53,857 --> 01:22:56,758
Use your spotlight as a
target and drop the gadget.

2252
01:22:56,758 --> 01:22:57,591
- [Mike] No!

2253
01:22:57,591 --> 01:22:58,424
- [VOiceover] You want me to land

2254
01:22:58,424 --> 01:22:59,257
and give you the trigger?

2255
01:22:59,257 --> 01:23:00,090
- Hell no!

2256
01:23:00,090 --> 01:23:01,298
- [Tom Servo] Sorry, just asking.

2257
01:23:01,298 --> 01:23:03,773
- I'm going to fire a flare
and you pull the trigger.

2258
01:23:03,773 --> 01:23:04,720
- [Mike] No!

2259
01:23:04,720 --> 01:23:06,303
- [Voiceover] Okay.

2260
01:23:07,299 --> 01:23:08,671
- Follow us, come on!

2261
01:23:08,671 --> 01:23:11,233
- She’s dressed like
an Elvis impersonator.

2262
01:23:11,233 --> 01:23:13,823
- [Tom Servo] If you see
only 10,000 movies this year,

2263
01:23:13,823 --> 01:23:16,573
make sure this isn't one of them.

2264
01:23:18,807 --> 01:23:20,921
- Soon Hitler’s giant mechanical spiders

2265
01:23:20,921 --> 01:23:23,277
had pushed past the Maginot Line.

2266
01:23:23,277 --> 01:23:25,694
- Jenny, I forgot the flares.

2267
01:23:27,440 --> 01:23:28,273
Here are the rig keys.

2268
01:23:28,273 --> 01:23:29,106
Would you get them?

2269
01:23:29,106 --> 01:23:29,939
- I'll get 'em.

2270
01:23:29,939 --> 01:23:32,266
- [Tom Servo] On the way to
shoot the flares, I forgot them.

2271
01:23:32,266 --> 01:23:33,506
- [Mike] A brilliant plot device,

2272
01:23:33,506 --> 01:23:36,256
forgetting to do a simple errand.

2273
01:23:40,949 --> 01:23:43,535
- These spiders have
lousy heaters, though.

2274
01:23:43,535 --> 01:23:45,056
- We've got to keep her
out of that black hole

2275
01:23:45,056 --> 01:23:46,437
until we make the drop.

2276
01:23:46,437 --> 01:23:47,749
- Okay, I'm going to try.

2277
01:23:47,749 --> 01:23:48,920
- Good boy.

2278
01:23:48,920 --> 01:23:53,087
- [Tom Servo] It’s like
Bigfoot in business casual.

2279
01:23:55,431 --> 01:23:56,749
- [Mike] The spider’s
gonna have a heart attack

2280
01:23:56,749 --> 01:23:58,217
from eating so many cheeseheads.

2281
01:23:58,217 --> 01:24:00,300
- Jog-walk out of danger!

2282
01:24:02,658 --> 01:24:06,825
- [Tom Servo] Uh, long line
is really cutting into me.

2283
01:24:08,248 --> 01:24:11,535
- [Mike] Might as well get
my Pall Malls while I’m here.

2284
01:24:11,535 --> 01:24:13,868
- (screams)

2285
01:24:15,758 --> 01:24:18,008
(shouting)

2286
01:24:20,223 --> 01:24:22,845
- Ah, God I hate paperwork!

2287
01:24:22,845 --> 01:24:23,678
Ahhh!

2288
01:24:24,963 --> 01:24:25,796
Ah!

2289
01:24:28,984 --> 01:24:30,692
- [Tom Servo] Hey, spider,
you have a ball hitch?

2290
01:24:30,692 --> 01:24:33,337
Mine is busted.
(gunshots)

2291
01:24:33,337 --> 01:24:37,504
- [Mike] I'm the twin brother
of Dutch, a man you murdered!

2292
01:24:39,634 --> 01:24:43,899
- [Tom Servo] Remember,
I mate, then I kill.

2293
01:24:43,899 --> 01:24:47,149
I'm going to squash your shoe under me.

2294
01:24:48,433 --> 01:24:49,266
- Bad spider!

2295
01:24:49,266 --> 01:24:50,099
Sit!

2296
01:24:50,099 --> 01:24:50,932
Bad!

2297
01:24:50,932 --> 01:24:52,780
- [Tom Servo] This man is
a brave, brave character

2298
01:24:52,780 --> 01:24:56,020
whom we've never seen before.

2299
01:24:56,020 --> 01:24:57,681
- [Mike] Normally I
stuff people in my butt,

2300
01:24:57,681 --> 01:25:01,858
but in your case I'll let
you come in the front way.

2301
01:25:01,858 --> 01:25:03,804
- Huh, another spider's
gonna have to come along

2302
01:25:03,804 --> 01:25:06,137
and give the guy a boost up.

2303
01:25:10,143 --> 01:25:10,976
- [Tom Servo] Oh boy,

2304
01:25:10,976 --> 01:25:14,543
he's carrying him like a loaf of bread.

2305
01:25:14,543 --> 01:25:17,189
And he drops him at the 10 yard line.

2306
01:25:17,189 --> 01:25:20,051
♫ I injected a paralyzing
toxin into the sheriff

2307
01:25:20,051 --> 01:25:24,218
♫ but I did not inject a
paralyzing toxin into the deputy ♫

2308
01:25:25,857 --> 01:25:29,817
- Oh no, he bit right into
the guy's fountain pen.

2309
01:25:29,817 --> 01:25:34,247
- [Tom Servo] And yet Bill
Rebane escapes unharmed.

2310
01:25:34,247 --> 01:25:35,640
- [Voiceover] I can't believe this thing.

2311
01:25:35,640 --> 01:25:38,723
- [Dr. Vance] It's as big as a house.

2312
01:25:39,606 --> 01:25:41,438
- [Mike] Oh crap, my shoe.

2313
01:25:41,438 --> 01:25:44,202
- [Dr. Langer] Vance, Vance!

2314
01:25:44,202 --> 01:25:45,414
- What happened?

2315
01:25:45,414 --> 01:25:47,229
- Spiders came out of the briefcase.

2316
01:25:47,229 --> 01:25:49,628
- [Tom Servo, Mike,
Crow] (groan disgustedly)

2317
01:25:49,628 --> 01:25:51,008
- Give me this, come on!

2318
01:25:51,008 --> 01:25:52,958
Get over there and take cover.

2319
01:25:52,958 --> 01:25:54,749
Hey, come on!

2320
01:25:54,749 --> 01:25:56,544
Everybody get out of there!

2321
01:25:56,544 --> 01:25:57,918
Hurry up, come on!

2322
01:25:57,918 --> 01:25:58,770
- [Tom Servo] Quit picking tobacco,

2323
01:25:58,770 --> 01:26:02,937
we're making a movie here,
ya damn migrant workers.

2324
01:26:05,528 --> 01:26:06,486
- Get down!

2325
01:26:06,486 --> 01:26:08,486
- [Tom Servo] Get funky!

2326
01:26:12,549 --> 01:26:14,132
- Ah, the firework.

2327
01:26:16,398 --> 01:26:18,698
- [Tom Servo] And the
blast was felt yards away.

2328
01:26:18,698 --> 01:26:20,522
- [Mike] The first extremely tentative

2329
01:26:20,522 --> 01:26:22,689
atomic test at Alamogordo.

2330
01:26:24,466 --> 01:26:26,049
- What?

2331
01:26:26,049 --> 01:26:26,882
- Alright.

2332
01:26:28,322 --> 01:26:30,308
- [Tom Servo] I am death,
destroyer of lawns.

2333
01:26:30,308 --> 01:26:34,238
- [Mike] Spider must've been really wet.

2334
01:26:34,238 --> 01:26:35,558
- But I came with knowledge

2335
01:26:35,558 --> 01:26:39,152
for a cheap clean
alternative to fossil fuel.

2336
01:26:39,152 --> 01:26:41,741
- [Tom Servo] Remember, don't
put your spider in a microwave

2337
01:26:41,741 --> 01:26:43,908
if you wrap it in tinfoil.

2338
01:26:45,892 --> 01:26:48,142
- Blah, they need a bucket.

2339
01:26:49,398 --> 01:26:53,270
- [Tom Servo] It came
from planet Gross Out.

2340
01:26:53,270 --> 01:26:56,155
Blah, I ate too much ice cream.

2341
01:26:56,155 --> 01:26:59,072
- [Mike] The spider needs a Zantac.

2342
01:26:59,948 --> 01:27:03,121
- Alan Hale digests a kielbasa.

2343
01:27:03,121 --> 01:27:05,371
(laughing)

2344
01:27:08,239 --> 01:27:10,364
(fake screaming)

2345
01:27:10,364 --> 01:27:11,447
- [Tom Servo] I guess somebody tampered

2346
01:27:11,447 --> 01:27:13,864
in God's domain or something.

2347
01:27:23,498 --> 01:27:26,492
- [Crow] Remember don't buy
margarine, only creamery butter.

2348
01:27:26,492 --> 01:27:29,001
[Preacher] When Pharaoh
refused the children of Israel

2349
01:27:29,001 --> 01:27:31,827
their right to exodus,
the heavens opened up

2350
01:27:31,827 --> 01:27:35,994
and deluged the land with
flies, frogs, lice and locusts.

2351
01:27:38,206 --> 01:27:41,155
It happened before and
it will happen again.

2352
01:27:41,155 --> 01:27:44,977
- [Mike] And now we'll
pass the collection plate.

2353
01:27:44,977 --> 01:27:46,674
- Guys, I think we're deep into

2354
01:27:46,674 --> 01:27:49,007
film student territory here.

2355
01:27:50,508 --> 01:27:53,203
- [Tom Servo] And Andrea
Scharf begat Kevin Brodie,

2356
01:27:53,203 --> 01:27:55,687
who begat Alan Rebane

2357
01:27:55,687 --> 01:27:56,645
- I think the problem was

2358
01:27:56,645 --> 01:28:00,128
that there weren't enough
Rebanes in this movie.

2359
01:28:00,128 --> 01:28:04,950
- [Tom Servo] The Brodie to
Rebane ratio is a little rich.

2360
01:28:04,950 --> 01:28:09,728
- [Mike] What if Buck Gillett
were the best a man could get?

2361
01:28:09,728 --> 01:28:11,862
- You know when Barbara
Hale won her Oscar for this,

2362
01:28:11,862 --> 01:28:14,775
she made a touching speech
where she said, in effect,

2363
01:28:14,775 --> 01:28:15,775
"Daheyyyae!"

2364
01:28:16,765 --> 01:28:18,397
- [Tom Servo] The filmmaker
gratefully acknowledges

2365
01:28:18,397 --> 01:28:19,965
the cooperation of the Gobbler,

2366
01:28:19,965 --> 01:28:23,037
the G. Heileman Brewing Company,
the Doughboy Corporation,

2367
01:28:23,037 --> 01:28:26,151
Fort Howard toilet paper,
Plochman’s Mustard Company,

2368
01:28:26,151 --> 01:28:28,807
the BoDeans, the American
Dairy Association,

2369
01:28:28,807 --> 01:28:31,775
and the Wisconsin chapter
of Wisconsin Dairy Farmers.

2370
01:28:31,775 --> 01:28:33,692
And the Violent Femmes.

2371
01:28:35,203 --> 01:28:37,600
- Like this film had a worldwide release.

2372
01:28:37,600 --> 01:28:38,791
- [Tom Servo] Dedicated to the memory

2373
01:28:38,791 --> 01:28:40,958
of Crazylegs Elroy Hirsch.

2374
01:28:42,192 --> 01:28:43,859
- [Mike] Go Packers.

2375
01:28:46,069 --> 01:28:46,913
(bang)

2376
01:28:46,913 --> 01:28:48,913
(creak)

2377
01:28:52,928 --> 01:28:53,886
(bang)

2378
01:28:53,886 --> 01:28:56,803
(metal screeching)

2379
01:28:58,209 --> 01:28:59,430
- We got pods everywhere.

2380
01:28:59,430 --> 01:29:02,093
Come on, come on, you're not, oh!

2381
01:29:02,093 --> 01:29:03,777
Crow, thank goodness it's you.

2382
01:29:03,777 --> 01:29:05,217
Hey I think it's just you and me.

2383
01:29:05,217 --> 01:29:06,569
I think we're the only normal ones left.

2384
01:29:06,569 --> 01:29:07,527
(screaming)

2385
01:29:07,527 --> 01:29:08,360
No!

2386
01:29:08,360 --> 01:29:09,193
Oh my God!

2387
01:29:09,193 --> 01:29:10,178
Bobo we have to do something!

2388
01:29:10,178 --> 01:29:12,845
Please tell me you're not a pod!

2389
01:29:14,054 --> 01:29:14,887
- Who me?

2390
01:29:14,887 --> 01:29:16,068
No.

2391
01:29:16,068 --> 01:29:18,465
Everyone else is down here, not me.

2392
01:29:18,465 --> 01:29:20,363
You want to know why not me?

2393
01:29:20,363 --> 01:29:22,416
Because a monkey isn't good enough.

2394
01:29:22,416 --> 01:29:23,526
Again!

2395
01:29:23,526 --> 01:29:25,041
Should we assimilate the monkey?

2396
01:29:25,041 --> 01:29:25,874
No!

2397
01:29:25,874 --> 01:29:27,524
The monkey's got a red butt.

2398
01:29:27,524 --> 01:29:28,987
Stupid monkey's got a red butt.

2399
01:29:28,987 --> 01:29:31,320
Does the monkey want a banana?

2400
01:29:31,320 --> 01:29:34,041
It takes its toll Mike.

2401
01:29:34,041 --> 01:29:35,343
- Would you please forget about all that?

2402
01:29:35,343 --> 01:29:37,691
Look the universe is in peril
and you have to save it.

2403
01:29:37,691 --> 01:29:39,697
The way I figure it, there's
got to be a mother pod

2404
01:29:39,697 --> 01:29:40,884
down there somewhere.

2405
01:29:40,884 --> 01:29:41,717
- [Crow, Tom Servo] (screeching)

2406
01:29:41,717 --> 01:29:42,550
- Geez!

2407
01:29:44,651 --> 01:29:47,000
- Who me save the galaxy?

2408
01:29:47,000 --> 01:29:49,242
Mike, I'm a stupid monkey.

2409
01:29:49,242 --> 01:29:50,639
I might as well admit it,

2410
01:29:50,639 --> 01:29:52,362
and I do have a red butt.

2411
01:29:52,362 --> 01:29:53,921
Let's face facts.

2412
01:29:53,921 --> 01:29:55,510
You ever seen my butt?

2413
01:29:55,510 --> 01:29:58,510
Here, take a good look at my butt.

2414
01:29:58,510 --> 01:29:59,343
- [Crow, Tom Servo] (squealing)

2415
01:29:59,343 --> 01:30:01,326
- Bobo listen, you can do it.

2416
01:30:01,326 --> 01:30:03,490
Hold on a second, just get.

2417
01:30:03,490 --> 01:30:06,636
See, see ball, see, see, go.

2418
01:30:06,636 --> 01:30:08,698
Listen to me, you've got
to find the mother pod

2419
01:30:08,698 --> 01:30:09,743
and destroy it.

2420
01:30:09,743 --> 01:30:10,576
You can do it.

2421
01:30:10,576 --> 01:30:13,146
You are a magnificent mountain gorilla.

2422
01:30:13,146 --> 01:30:15,546
You are Bobo, son of Coco.

2423
01:30:15,546 --> 01:30:18,963
- Yes and heir to the great lineage Godo!

2424
01:30:20,319 --> 01:30:21,674
Mogo!

2425
01:30:21,674 --> 01:30:22,841
And Chim Chim!

2426
01:30:25,031 --> 01:30:26,925
Now where's that mother pod?

2427
01:30:26,925 --> 01:30:28,008
(pod screeching)

2428
01:30:28,008 --> 01:30:30,258
(grunting)

2429
01:30:38,573 --> 01:30:41,823
(celebratory shouting)

2430
01:30:43,737 --> 01:30:44,794
- Yes.

2431
01:30:44,794 --> 01:30:46,375
- Mike, are you okay?

2432
01:30:46,375 --> 01:30:47,482
- Mike are you alright?

2433
01:30:47,482 --> 01:30:48,315
- Yeah, yeah I'm okay.

2434
01:30:48,315 --> 01:30:49,148
How about you?

2435
01:30:49,148 --> 01:30:50,340
- We're okay too.

2436
01:30:50,340 --> 01:30:51,816
They had us locked up.

2437
01:30:51,816 --> 01:30:53,149
Ah, you big lug.

2438
01:30:53,149 --> 01:30:55,035
All I can say is (screeches)

2439
01:30:55,035 --> 01:30:55,868
- Aah!

2440
01:30:57,821 --> 01:30:59,315
- [Crow] I was kidding.

2441
01:30:59,315 --> 01:31:01,475
- Well I'm not sure.

2442
01:31:01,475 --> 01:31:03,956
- Well I guess we just
gotta get the dried husks

2443
01:31:03,956 --> 01:31:06,485
of our dooplegangers out of here.

2444
01:31:06,485 --> 01:31:08,728
- Back to you Bobo.

2445
01:31:08,728 --> 01:31:11,362
♫ Hooga shaka, hooga hooga hooga shaka,

2446
01:31:11,362 --> 01:31:13,904
♫ hooga hooga hooga shaka hooga ♫

2447
01:31:13,904 --> 01:31:16,150
- Oh Lawgiver, I saved you!

2448
01:31:16,150 --> 01:31:18,472
I'm so glad to see you.

2449
01:31:18,472 --> 01:31:20,987
- Bobo, get your paws off me.

2450
01:31:20,987 --> 01:31:22,739
Have you been drinking?

2451
01:31:22,739 --> 01:31:25,072
No, look see here's dead you

2452
01:31:26,045 --> 01:31:29,193
and Observer here's dead pod you.

2453
01:31:29,193 --> 01:31:31,308
You see, all the time they
were watching the movie,

2454
01:31:31,308 --> 01:31:32,790
you were a pod.

2455
01:31:32,790 --> 01:31:36,624
I saved you and the whole
galaxy, I'm so proud.

2456
01:31:36,624 --> 01:31:38,513
- You mean, they watched the movie

2457
01:31:38,513 --> 01:31:42,506
and I didn't get to watch
them watching the movie?

2458
01:31:42,506 --> 01:31:44,206
Bobo get rid of my body.

2459
01:31:44,206 --> 01:31:46,735
Brain guy, send them the movie.

2460
01:31:46,735 --> 01:31:49,402
Again. (laughs)

2461
01:31:50,497 --> 01:31:54,664
- [Tom Servo, Mike, Crow]
Movie-cide again! (crying)

2462
01:31:55,724 --> 01:31:59,474
(peaceful synthesizer music)

2463
01:32:52,781 --> 01:32:54,830
- (blows raspberry)

